\id EZK - Brenton English Septuagint 
\h Ezekiel 
\toc1 Ezekiel 
\toc2 Ezekiel 
\toc3 Ezek. 
\mt1 EZEKIEL 
\c 1 
\p
\v 1 Now it happened in the thirtieth year, in the fourth month, on the fifth day of the month, that I was among the captivity by the river of Chobar; and the heavens were opened, and I saw visions of God. 
\v 2 On the fifth day of the month; this was the fifth year of the captivity of king Joakim. 
\v 3 The word of the Lord came to Ezekiel the priest, the son of Buzi, in the land of the Chaldeans, by the river of Chobar; and the hand of the Lord was upon me. 
\p
\v 4 I looked, and, behold, a sweeping wind came from the north, and a great cloud on it, and \add there was\add* brightness all around it, and gleaming fire, and among it as it were the appearance of amber among the fire, and brightness in it. 
\p
\v 5 In the midst as it were the likeness of four living creatures. And this was their appearance; the likeness of a man was upon them. 
\v 6 Each one \add had\add* four faces, and each one \add had\add* four wings. 
\v 7 Their legs were straight; and their feet were winged, and \add there were\add* sparks, like gleaming brass, and their wings were light. 
\v 8 The hand of a man was under their wings on their four sides. 
\v 9 The faces of them four didn't turn when they went; they went every one straight forward. 
\v 10 The likeness of their faces: the face of a man, and the face of a lion on the right for all four; and the face of a calf on the left for all four; and the face of an eagle for all four. 
\v 11 The four had their wings spread out above; each one \add had\add* two joined to one another, and two covered their bodies. 
\v 12 Each one went straight forward: wherever the spirit was going they went, and didn't turn back. 
\p
\v 13 Among the living creatures \add there was\add* something like burning coals of fire, like the appearance of lamps moving among the living creatures; and there was brightness of fire, and out of the fire came forth lightning. 
\p
\v 15 I looked, and, behold, the four \add had each\add* one wheel on the ground near the living creatures. 
\v 16 The appearance of the wheels was as the appearance of beryl: and the four had one likeness: and their work was as it were a wheel in a wheel. 
\v 17 They went on their four sides: they didn't turn as they went; 
\v 18 neither did their backs \add turn\add*: and they were high: and I beheld them, and the backs of them four were full of eyes all around. 
\p
\v 19 When the living creatures went, the wheels went by them: and when the living creatures lifted themselves off the earth, the wheels were lifted off. 
\v 20 Wherever the cloud happened to be, there was the spirit ready to go: the wheels went and were lifted up with them; because the spirit of life was in the wheels. 
\v 21 When those went, \add the wheels\add* went; and when those stood, \add the wheels\add* stood; and when those lifted themselves off the earth, they were lifted off with them: for the spirit of life was in the wheels. 
\p
\v 22 There was a likeness over the heads of the living creatures, like an expanse, like the appearance of crystal, stretched out above their wings above. 
\v 23 Their wings were spread out under the expanse, reaching one to the other; two \add wings\add* to each, covering their bodies. 
\v 24 I heard the sound of their wings when they went, as the sound of much water: and when they stood, their wings were let down. 
\p
\v 25 Lo! A voice from above the expanse 
\v 26 that was over their head, \add there was\add* as the appearance of a sapphire stone, \add and\add* the likeness of a throne upon it: and upon the likeness of the throne was the likeness as an appearance of a man above. 
\v 27 I saw as it were the resemblance of amber from the appearance of the loins and upwards, and from the appearance of the loins and under I saw an appearance of fire, and the brightness of it all around. 
\v 28 As the appearance of a rainbow when it is in the cloud on a rainy day, so was the form of the brightness all around. 
\c 2 
\p
\v 1 This was the appearance of the likeness of the glory of the Lord. I saw and fell upon my face, and heard a voice speaking: and he said to me, Son of man, stand upon your feet, and I will speak to you. 
\p
\v 2 The Spirit came upon me, and took me up, and raised me, and set me on my feet: and I heard him speaking to me. 
\v 3 He said to me, Son of man, I send you forth to the house of Israel, those who provoke me; who have provoked me, they and their fathers, to this day. 
\v 4 You will say to them, Thus says the Lord. 
\v 5 Whether then indeed they will hear or fear, (for it is a rebellious house,) yet they will know that you are a prophet among them. 
\p
\v 6 You, son of man, don't be afraid them, nor be dismayed at their \f + \fr 2:6 \fqa Gr. \ft face.\f*presence; (for they will rage against you and gather around you, and you dwell among scorpions. Don't be afraid of their words, nor be dismayed before them; for they are a rebellious house. 
\v 7 You will speak my words to them, whether they will hear or fear: for it is a rebellious house. 
\p
\v 8 You, son of man, hear him who speaks to you; don't be rebellious, like the rebellious house: open your mouth, and eat what I give you. 
\v 9 I looked, and behold, a hand stretched out to me, and in it a volume of a book. 
\v 10 He unrolled it before me: and in it the front and the back were written \add upon\add*: and there was written \add in it\add* Lamentation, and mournful song, and woe. 
\c 3 
\p
\v 1 He said to me, Son of man, eat this volume, and go and speak to the children of Israel. 
\v 2 So he opened my mouth, and caused me to eat the volume. 
\p And he said to me, Son of man, 
\v 3 your mouth will eat, and your belly will be filled with this volume that is given to you. So I ate it; and it was in my mouth as sweet honey. 
\p
\v 4 He said to me, Son of man, go your way, and go in to the house of Israel, and speak my words to them. 
\v 5 For you are not sent to a people of obscure speech and difficult language, \add but\add* to the house of Israel; 
\v 6 neither to many nations of other speech and other tongues, nor of harsh language, whose words you would not understand: although if I \add had\add* sent you to such, they would have listened to you. 
\v 7 But the house of Israel will not be willing to listen to you; for they will not listen to me: for all the house of Israel are stubborn and hard-hearted. 
\v 8 And, behold, I have made your face strong against their faces, and I will strengthen your opposition against their opposition. 
\v 9 It will be continually stronger than a rock: don't be afraid of them, neither be dismayed at their faces, because it is a rebellious house. 
\p
\v 10 He said to me, Son of man, receive into your heart all the words that I have spoken to you, and hear \add them\add* with your ears. 
\v 11 Go your way, go in to the captivity, to the children of your people, and you will speak to them, and say to them, Thus says the Lord; whether they will hear, \add or\add* whether they will yield. 
\p
\v 12 Then the Spirit took me up, and I heard behind me the voice \add as\add* of a great earthquake, \add saying\add*, Blessed \add be\add* the glory of the Lord from his place. 
\v 13 I perceived the sound of the wings of the living creatures clapping one to the other, and the sound of the wheels was near them, and the sound of the earthquake. 
\v 14 The Spirit lifted me, and took me up, and I went in the impulse of my spirit; and the hand of the Lord was mighty upon me. 
\p
\v 15 Then I passed through the air and came into the captivity, and went round \add to\add* those who dwelt by the river of Chobar who were there; and I sat there seven days, living among them. 
\p
\v 16 After the seven days the word of the Lord came to me, saying, Son of man, 
\v 17 I have made you a watchman to the house of Israel; and you will hear a word of my mouth, and give them warning them from me. 
\v 18 When I say to the wicked, You will surely die; and you have not instructed him, to give instruction to the wicked, to turn from his ways, that he should live; that wicked man will die in his wickedness; but his blood will I require at your hand. 
\v 19 But if you instruct the wicked, and he doesn't turn from his wickedness, and from his way, that wicked man will die in his wickedness, but you will deliver your soul. 
\p
\v 20 When the righteous turns away from his righteousness, and commits a trespass, and I will bring punishment before him, he will die, because you did not instruct him: he will even die in his sins, because his righteousness will not be remembered; but his blood I will require at your hand. 
\v 21 But if you instruct the righteous not to sin, and he doesn't sin, the righteous will surely live, because you have instructed him; and you will deliver your own soul. 
\p
\v 22 The hand of the Lord came upon me; and he said to me, Arise, and go forth into the plain, and there you will be spoken to. 
\p
\v 23 I arose, and went out to the plain: and, behold, the glory of the Lord stood there, according to the vision, and according to the glory of the Lord, which I saw by the river of Chobar: and I fell on my face. 
\v 24 Then the Spirit came upon me, and set me on my feet, and spoke to me, and said to me, Go in, and shut yourself up in your house. 
\v 25 And you, son of man, behold, bonds are prepared for you, and they will bind you with them, and you will not go out from them. 
\v 26 Also I will bind your tongue, and you will be dumb, and will not be to them a reprover: because it is a rebellious house. 
\v 27 But when I speak to you, I will open your mouth, and you will say to them, Thus says the Lord, He who hears, let him hear; and he who is disobedient, let him be disobedient: because it is a rebellious house. 
\c 4 
\p
\v 1 You, son of man, take a brick, and you will set it in front of you, and portray on it the city, \add even\add* Jerusalem. 
\v 2 You will besiege it, and build works against it, and throw up a mound all around it, and pitch camps against it, and set up engines all around. 
\v 3 Take to yourself an iron pan, and you will set it \add for\add* an iron wall between you and the city: and you will set your face against it, and it will be in a siege, and you will besiege it. This is a sign to the children of Israel. 
\p
\v 4 You will lie upon your left side, and lay the iniquities of the house of Israel upon it, according to the number of the hundred and fifty days \add during\add* which you will lie upon it: and you will bear their iniquities. 
\v 5 For I have appointed you their iniquities for a number of days, for a hundred and ninety days: so you will bear the iniquities of the house of Israel. 
\v 6 You will accomplish this, and \add then\add* will lie on your right side, and will bear the iniquities of the house of Judah forty days: I have appointed you a day for a year. 
\p
\v 7 So you will set your face to the siege of Jerusalem, and will strengthen your arm, and will prophesy against it. 
\v 8 And, behold, I have prepared bonds for you, and you may not turn from your one side to the other, until the days of your siege will be accomplished. 
\p
\v 9 Also take to yourself wheat, and barley, and beans, and lentiles, and millet, and bread-grain; and you will cast them into an earthen vessel, and will make them into loaves for yourself; and you will eat them a hundred and ninety days, according to the number of the days \add during\add* which you sleep on your side. 
\v 10 You will eat your food by weight, twenty shekels a day: from time to time you will eat them. 
\v 11 You will drink water by measure, even from time to time you will drink the sixth part of a hin. 
\v 12 You will eat them \add as\add* a barley cake: you will bake them before their eyes over human dung. 
\p
\v 13 You will say, Thus says the Lord God of Israel; Thus will the children of Israel eat unclean things among the nations. 
\v 14 Then I said, Not so, Lord God of Israel: surely my soul has not been defiled with uncleanness; nor have I eaten that which died of itself or was torn of beasts from my birth until now; neither has any corrupt flesh entered into my mouth. 
\p
\v 15 He said to me, Behold, I have given you dung of oxen instead of human dung, and you will prepare your loaves upon it. 
\p
\v 16 He said to me, Son of man, behold, I break the \f + \fr 4:16 \fqa Gr. \ft support. ``Support of bread'' is a Hebrew idiom for food supply.\f*supply of bread in Jerusalem: and they will eat bread by weight and in want; and will drink water by measure, and in a state of ruin: 
\v 17 so they may lack bread and water; and a man and his brother will be consumed, and they will waste away in their iniquities. 
\c 5 
\p
\v 1 You, son of man, take you a sword sharper than a barber's razor; you will procure it for yourself, and will bring it upon your head, and upon your beard: and you will take a pair of scales, and will separate the hair. 
\v 2 A fourth part you will burn in the fire among the city, at the fulfilment of the days of the siege: and you will take a fourth part, and burn it up among it: and a fourth part you will cut with a sword all around it: and a fourth part you will scatter to the wind; and I will draw out a sword after them. 
\p
\v 3 You will take from there a few in number, and will wrap them in the fold of your garment. 
\v 4 You will take of these again, and cast them into the midst of the fire, and burn them up with fire: from from there will come forth fire; and you will say to the whole house of Israel, 
\p
\v 5 Thus says the Lord; This is Jerusalem: I have set her and the lands all around her among the nations. 
\v 6 You will declare my ordinances to the lawless one from out of the nations; and my statutes \add to the sinful one\add* of the lands all around her: because they have rejected my ordinances, and have not walked in my statutes. 
\p
\v 7 Therefore thus says the Lord, Because your occasion \add for sin has been taken\add* from the nations all around you, and you have not walked in my statutes, nor kept my ordinances, no, you have not even done according to the ordinances of the nations all around you; therefore thus says the Lord; 
\v 8 Behold, I am against you, and I will execute judgment among you in the sight of the nations. 
\v 9 I will do in you things which I have not done, and the like of which I will not do again, for all your abominations. 
\v 10 Therefore the fathers will eat \add their\add* children among you, and children will eat \add their\add* fathers; and I will execute judgments in you, and I will scatter all that are left of you to every wind. 
\p
\v 11 Therefore, \add as\add* I live, says the Lord; surely, because you have defiled my holy things with all your abominations, I also will reject you; my eye will not spare, and I will have no mercy. 
\v 12 A fourth part of you will be cut off by pestilence, and a fourth part of you will be consumed among you with famine: and \add as for another\add* fourth part of you, I will scatter them to every wind; and a fourth part of you will fall by the sword all around you, and I will draw out a sword after them. 
\p
\v 13 My wrath and my anger will be accomplished upon them: and you will know that I the Lord have spoken in my zeal, when I have accomplished my anger upon them. 
\p
\v 14 I will make you desolate, and your daughters all around you, in the sight of every one that passes through. 
\v 15 You will be mourned over and miserable among the nations all around you, when I have executed judgments in you in the vengeance of my wrath. I the Lord have spoken. 
\v 16 When I have sent against them shafts of famine, then they will be consumed, and I will break the strength of your bread. 
\v 17 So I will send forth against you famine and wild beasts, and I will punish you; and death and blood will pass through you; and I will bring a sword upon you all around. I the Lord have spoken. 
\c 6 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, set your face against the mountains of Israel, and prophesy against them; 
\v 3 and you will say, 
\p You mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord; thus says the Lord to the mountains, and to the hills, and to the valleys, and to the forests; Behold, I bring a sword upon you, and your high places will be completely destroyed. 
\v 4 Your altars will be broken to pieces, and your sanctuaries; and I will cast down your killed \add men\add* before your idols. 
\v 5 I will scatter your bones all around your altars, 
\v 6 and in all your habitations: the cities will be made desolate, and the high places completely laid waste; that your altars may be destroyed, and your idols be broken to pieces, and your sanctuaries be abolished. 
\v 7 Killed \add men\add* will fall among you, and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 8 When there are \add some\add* of you escaping from the sword among the nations, and when you are scattered in the lands; 
\v 9 then those of you who escape among the nations where they were carried captive will remember me; I have sworn \add an oath\add* against their heart that goes playing the prostitute from me, and their eyes that go playing the prostitute after their practices; and they will mourn over themselves for all their abominations. 
\v 10 They will know that I the Lord have spoken. 
\p
\v 11 Thus says the Lord; Clap with \add your\add* hand, and stamp with \add your\add* foot and say, Ah, ah! For all the abominations of the house of Israel: they will fall by the sword, and by pestilence, and by famine. 
\v 12 He who is near will fall by the sword; and he who is far off will die by the pestilence; and he who is in the siege will be consumed with famine: and I will accomplish my anger upon them. 
\p
\v 13 Then you will know that I am the Lord, when your killed are among your idols all around your altars, on every high hill, and under \add every\add* shady tree, where they offered a sweet savour to all their idols. 
\v 14 I will stretch out my hand against them, and I will make the land desolate and ruined from the wilderness of Deblatha, in all their habitations: \add and\add* you will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 7 
\p
\v 1 Moreover the word of the Lord came to me, saying, Also, you, son of man, say, 
\v 2 Thus says the Lord; 
\p An end has come to the land of Israel, the end has come on the four corners of the land. 
\v 3 The end has come 
\v 4 on you, the inhabitant of the land: the time has come, the day has drawn near, not with tumult, nor with pangs. 
\p
\v 5 Now I will pour out my anger upon you near at hand, and I will accomplish my wrath on you: and I will judge you for your ways, and repay you for all your abominations. 
\v 6 My eye will not spare, nor will I have any mercy: for I will repay you for your ways, and your abominations will be among you; and you will know that I am the Lord who strike \add you\add*. 
\v 7 Now the end \add has come\add* to you, and I will send \add judgment\add* upon you: and I will take vengeance for your ways, and will repay you for all your abominations. 
\v 8 My eye will not spare, nor will I have any mercy: for I will repay you for your way, and your abominations will be among you; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 9 For thus says the Lord; Behold, the end has come. 
\p
\v 10 Behold, the day of the Lord! Although the rod has blossomed, 
\v 11 pride has sprung up, and will break the staff of the wicked one, and \add that\add* not with tumult, nor with haste. 
\v 12 The time has come, behold the day: don't let the buyer rejoice, and don't let the seller mourn. 
\v 13 For the buyer will never again return to the seller, neither will a man cling with the eye \add of hope\add* to his life. 
\v 14 Sound the trumpet, and pass sentence on all together. 
\v 15 \add There will be\add* war with the sword outside, and famine and pestilence inside: he who is in the field will die by the sword; and famine and pestilence will destroy those who are in the city. 
\p
\v 16 But those who escape from them will escape and be on the mountains: and I will kill them all, every one for his iniquities. 
\v 17 All hands will be completely weakened, and all thighs will be defiled with moisture. 
\v 18 They will gird themselves with sackcloth, and amazement will cover them; and shame will be upon them, \add even\add* upon every face, and baldness upon every head. 
\v 19 Their silver will be cast forth in the streets, and their gold will be despised: their souls will not be satisfied, and their bellies will not be filled: for it was the punishment of their iniquities. 
\v 20 \add As for\add* their choice ornaments, they employed them for pride, and from them they made images of their abominations: therefore have I made them uncleanness to them. 
\p
\v 21 I will deliver them into the hands of strangers to make them a prey, and to the pests of the earth for a spoil; and they will profane them. 
\v 22 I will turn away my face from them, and they will defile my charge, and will go in to them unguardedly, and profane them. 
\v 23 They will work uncleanness: because the land is full of foreign nations, and the city is full of wickedness. 
\v 24 I will turn back the boasting of their strength; and their holy things will be defiled. 
\v 25 And \add though\add* atonement will come, and \add one\add* will seek peace, yet there will be none. 
\v 26 There will be woe upon woe, and there will be message upon message; and a vision will be sought from a prophet; but the law will perish from the priest, and counsel from the elders. 
\v 27 The prince will clothe himself with desolation, and the hands of the people of the land will be made feeble: I will do to them according to their ways, and according to their judgments will I punish them; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 8 
\p
\v 1 It happened in the sixth year, in the fifth month, on the fifth \add day\add* of the month, I was sitting in the house, and the elders of Judah were sitting before me: and the hand of the Lord came upon me. 
\v 2 I looked, and, behold, the likeness of a man: from his loins and downwards \add there was\add* fire, and from his loins upwards \add there was\add* as the appearance of amber. 
\v 3 He stretched forth the likeness of a hand, and took me up by the crown of my head; and the Spirit lifted me up between the earth and sky, and brought me to Jerusalem in a vision of God, to the porch of the gate that looks to the north, where was the pillar of the Purchaser. 
\v 4 And, behold, the glory of the Lord God of Israel was there, according to the vision which I saw in the plain. 
\p
\v 5 He said to me, Son of man, lift up your eyes toward the north. So I lifted up my eyes toward the north, and, behold, \add I looked\add* from the north toward the eastern gate. 
\v 6 He said to me, Son of man, have you seen what these do? They commit great abominations here so that I should keep away from my sanctuary: and you will see yet greater iniquities. 
\p
\v 7 He brought me to the porch of the court. 
\v 8 He said to me, Son of man, dig: so I dug, and behold a door. 
\v 9 He said to me, Go in, and behold the iniquities which they practise here. 
\v 10 So I went in and looked; and beheld vain abominations, and all the idols of the house of Israel, portrayed upon them all around. 
\v 11 Seventy men of the elders of the house of Israel, and Jechonias the son of Saphan stood in their presence among them, and each one held his censer in his hand; and the smoke of the incense went up. 
\v 12 He said to me, You have seen, son of man, what the elders of the house of Israel do, each one of them in their secret chamber: because they have said, The Lord doesn't see; The Lord has forsaken the earth. 
\p
\v 13 He said to me, You will see yet greater iniquities which these do. 
\v 14 He brought me in to the porch of the house of the Lord that looks to the north; and, behold, \add there were\add* women sitting there lamenting for Thammuz. 
\v 15 He said to me, Son of man, you have seen; but you will yet see \add evil\add* practices greater than these. 
\p
\v 16 He brought me into the inner court of the house of the Lord, and at the entrance of the temple of the Lord, between the porch and the altar, were about twenty men, with their back parts toward the temple of the Lord, and their faces \add turned\add* the opposite way; and these were worshipping the sun. 
\v 17 He said to me, Son of man, you have seen this. \add Is it\add* a little thing to the house of Judah to practise the iniquities which they have practised here? For they have filled the land with wickedness: and, behold, these are as scorners. 
\v 18 Therefore will I deal with them in wrath: my eye will not spare, nor will I have any mercy. 
\c 9 
\p
\v 1 He cried in my ears with a loud voice, saying, The judgment of the city has drawn near; and each had the weapons of destruction in his hand. 
\v 2 And, behold, six men came from the way of the high gate that looks toward the north, and each one's axe was in his hand; and there was one man among them clothed with a long robe down to the feet, and a sapphire girdle was on his loins: and they came in and stood near the bronze altar. 
\v 3 The glory of the God of Israel, that was upon them, went up from the cherubs to the porch of the house. 
\p And he called the man who was clothed with the long robe, who had the girdle on his loins; 
\v 4 and said to him, Go through the midst of Jerusalem, and set a mark on the foreheads of the men who groan and that grieve for all the iniquities that are done among them. 
\v 5 He said to the first in my hearing, Go after him into the city, and strike: and don't let your eyes spare, and have no mercy. 
\v 6 Kill completely old man and youth, and virgin, and infants, and women: but don't you go near any on whom is the mark: begin at my sanctuary. 
\p So they began with the elder men who were within in the house. 
\v 7 He said to them, Defile the house, and go out and fill the ways with dead bodies, and strike. 
\p
\v 8 It happened as they were striking, that I fell upon my face, and cried out, and said, Alas, O Lord! Will you destroy the remnant of Israel, in pouring out your wrath upon Jerusalem? 
\v 9 Then said he to me, The wickedness of the house of Israel and Judah has become very exceedingly great: for the land is filled with many nations, and the city is filled with wickedness and uncleanness: because they have said, The Lord has forsaken the earth, The Lord doesn't look on \add it\add*. 
\v 10 Therefore my eye will not spare, neither will I have any mercy: I have repayed their ways upon their heads. 
\p
\v 11 And, behold, the man clothed with the long robe, and wearing the girdle about his loins, answered and said, I have done as you commanded me. 
\c 10 
\p
\v 1 Then I looked, and, behold, over the expanse that was above the head of the cherubs \add there was\add* a likeness of a throne over them, as a sapphire stone. 
\v 2 He said to the man clothed with the \add long\add* robe, Go in between the wheels that are under the cherubs, and fill your hands with coals of fire from between the cherubs, and scatter \add them\add* over the city. And he went in in my sight. 
\p
\v 3 The cherubs stood on the right hand of the house, as the man went in; and the cloud filled the inner court. 
\v 4 Then the glory of the Lord departed from the cherubs to the porch of the house; and the cloud filled the house, and the court was filled with the brightness of the glory of the Lord. 
\v 5 The sound of the cherubs' wings was heard as far as the outer court, as the voice of the Almighty God speaking. 
\p
\v 6 It happened, when he gave a charge to the man clothed with the sacred robe, saying, Take fire from between the wheels from between the cherubs, that he went in, and stood near the wheels. 
\v 7 He stretched forth his hand into the midst of the fire that was between the cherubs, and took \add of it\add*, and put \add it\add* into the hands of the man clothed with the sacred robe: and he took \add it\add*, and went out. 
\p
\v 8 I saw the cherubs \add having\add* the likeness of men's hands under their wings. 
\v 9 I saw, and behold, four wheels stood by the cherubs, one wheel by each cherub: and the appearance of the wheels was as the appearance of a carbuncle stone. 
\v 10 And \add as for\add* their appearance, \add there was\add* one likeness to the four, as if there should be a wheel among a wheel. 
\v 11 When they went, they went on their four sides; they didn't turn when they went, for whichever way the first head looked, they went; and they didn't turn as they went. 
\v 12 Their backs, and their hands, and their wings, and the wheels, were full of eyes all around the four wheels. 
\v 13 These wheels were called Gelgel in my hearing. 
\v 15 The cherubs were the same living creature which I saw by the river of Chobar. 
\p
\v 16 When the cherubs went, the wheels went, and they were close to them: and when the cherubs lifted up their wings to mount up from the earth, their wheels didn't turn. 
\v 17 When they stood, \add the wheels\add* stood; and when they mounted up, \add the wheels\add* mounted up with them: because the spirit of life was in them. 
\p
\v 18 Then the glory of the Lord departed from the house, and went up on the cherubs. 
\v 19 The cherubs lifted up their wings, and mounted up from the earth in my sight: when they went out, the wheels were also beside them, and they stood at the entrance of the front gate of the house of the Lord; and the glory of the God of Israel was upon them above. 
\p
\v 20 This is the living creature which I saw under the God of Israel by the river of Chobar; and I knew that they were cherubs. 
\v 21 Each one \add had\add* four faces, and each one \add had\add* eight wings; and under their wings was the likeness of men's hands. 
\v 22 And \add as for\add* the likeness of their faces, these are the \add same\add* faces which I saw under the glory of the God of Israel by the river of Chobar: and they went each straight forward. 
\c 11 
\p
\v 1 Moreover the Spirit took me up, and brought me to the front gate of the house of the Lord, that looks eastward: and behold at the entrance of the gate were about twenty-five men; and I saw among them Jechonias the son of Ezer, and Phaltias the son of Banæas, the leaders of the people. 
\p
\v 2 The Lord said to me, Son of man, these are the men who devise vanities, and take evil counsel in this city: 
\v 3 who say, Have not the houses been newly built? This is the caldron, and we are the flesh. 
\v 4 Therefore prophesy against them, prophesy, son of man. 
\v 5 The Spirit of the Lord fell upon me, and said to me, say; 
\p Thus says the Lord; Thus have you said, O house of Israel: and I know the devices of your spirit. 
\v 6 You have multiplied your dead in this city, and you have filled your ways with killed men. 
\v 7 Therefore thus says the Lord; Your dead whom you have struck among it, these are the flesh, and this \add city\add* is the caldron: but I will bring you forth out of the midst of it. 
\v 8 You fear the sword; and I will bring a sword upon you, says the Lord. 
\v 9 I will bring you forth out of the midst of it, and will deliver you into the hands of strangers, and will execute judgments among you. 
\v 10 You will fall by the sword; I will judge you on the mountains of Israel; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 13 It happened, while I was prophesying, that Phaltias the son of Banæas died. And I fell upon my face, and cried with a loud voice, and said, Alas, alas, O Lord! Will you completely destroy the remnant of Israel? 
\v 14 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 15 Son of man, your brothers, and the men of your captivity, and all the house of Israel have come to the full, to whom the inhabitants of Jerusalem said, Keep far away from the Lord: the land is given to us for an inheritance. 
\v 16 Therefore say you, 
\p Thus says the Lord; I will cast them off among the nations, and will disperse them into every land, yet I will be to them for a little sanctuary in the lands which they will enter. 
\v 17 Therefore say, Thus says the Lord; I will also take them from the nations, and gather them out of the lands wherein I have scattered them, and will give them the land of Israel. 
\p
\v 18 They will enter in there, and will remove all the abominations of it, and all its iniquities from it. 
\v 19 I will give them another heart, and will put a new spirit within them; and will extract the heart of stone from their flesh, and give them a heart of flesh: 
\v 20 so they may walk in my commandments, and keep my ordinances, and do them: and they will be my people, and I will their God. 
\p
\v 21 As for the heart \add set upon\add* their abominations and their iniquities, as their heart went \add after them\add*, I have repayed their ways on their heads, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 22 Then the cherubs lifted up their wings, and the wheels beside them; and the glory of the God of Israel was over them above. 
\v 23 The glory of the Lord went up from the midst of the city, and stood on the mountain which was in front of the city. 
\p
\v 24 The Spirit took me up, and brought me to the land of the Chaldeans, to the captivity, in a vision by the Spirit of God: and I went up after the vision which I saw. 
\v 25 I spoke to the captivity all the words of the Lord which he had showed me. 
\c 12 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, you dwell among the iniquities of those, who have eyes to see, and don't see; and have ears to hear, and don't hear: because it is a rebellious house. 
\p
\v 3 You therefore, son of man, prepare yourself baggage for going into captivity by day in their sight; and you will be led into captivity from your place into another place in their sight; so they may see that it is a rebellious house. 
\v 4 You will carry forth your baggage, baggage for captivity, by day before their eyes: and you will go forth at evening, as a captive goes forth, in their sight. 
\v 5 Dig for yourself into the wall \add of the house\add*, and you will pass through it in their sight: 
\v 6 you will be lifted up on \add men's\add* shoulders, and will go forth in secret: you will cover your face, and will not see the ground: because I have made you a sign to the house of Israel. 
\p
\v 7 I did thus according to all that he commanded me; and I carried forth my baggage for captivity by day, and in the evening I dug through the wall for myself, and went out secretly; I was taken up on \add men's\add* shoulders before them. 
\v 8 The word of the Lord came to me in the morning, saying, 
\v 9 Son of man, have not the house of Israel, the rebellious house, said to you, What are you doing? 
\v 10 Say to them, 
\p Thus says the Lord God, the Prince and the Ruler in Israel, to all the house of Israel who are among them: 
\v 11 say, I am performing signs: as I have done, so will it be to them: they will go into banishment and captivity. 
\v 12 The prince among them will be borne upon shoulders, and will go forth in secret through the wall, and will dig so that he may go out that way: he will cover his face, that he may not be seen by \add any\add* eye, and he himself will not see the ground. 
\v 13 I will spread out my net over him, and he will be caught in my snare, and I will bring him to Babylon to the land of the Chaldeans; but he will not see it, though he will die there. 
\v 14 I will scatter to every wind all his assistants all around him, and all who help him; and I will draw out a sword after them. 
\v 15 They will know that I am the Lord, when I have scattered them among the nations; and I will disperse them in the lands. 
\p
\v 16 Yet I will leave a few of them, men escaping the sword, the famine, and death; so they may declare all their iniquities among the nations where they have gone; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 17 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 18 Son of man, eat your bread with sorrow, and drink \add your\add* water with torment and affliction. 
\v 19 You will say to the people of the land, Thus says the Lord to the inhabitants of Jerusalem on the land of Israel; They will eat their bread in scarcity, and will drink their water in desolation, that the land may be desolate with all that it contains: for all who dwell in it are ungodly. 
\v 20 Their inhabited cities will be laid completely waste, and the land will be desolate; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 21 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 22 Son of man, what is your parable on the land of Israel, that you say, The days are long, the vision has perished? 
\v 23 Therefore say to them, 
\p Thus says the Lord; I will even set aside this parable, and the house of Israel will no more at all use this parable: for you will say to them, The days are at hand, and the fulfillment of every vision. 
\v 24 For there will no more be any false vision, nor any one prophesying flatteries among the children of Israel. 
\v 25 For I the Lord will speak my words; I will speak and perform \add them\add*, and will no more delay, for in your days, O rebellious house, I will speak the word, and will perform \add it\add*, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 26 Moreover the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 27 Son of man, behold, the rebellious house of Israel boldly say, The vision which this man sees is for many days, and he prophesies for times afar off. 
\v 28 Therefore say to them, 
\p Thus says the Lord; From now on none of my words which I speak will linger: I will speak and do, says the Lord. 
\c 13 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, prophesy against the prophets of Israel, and you will prophesy, and will say to them, Hear the word of the Lord: 
\p
\v 3 Thus says the Lord, Woe to those who prophesy out of their own heart, and who see nothing at all. 
\v 4 Your prophets, O Israel, are like foxes in the deserts. 
\v 5 They did not stand in the breach, nor gather the flock for the house of Israel, those who say, In the day of the Lord, have not stood.
\v 6 They see falsehood and divine emptiness, who say, The Lord says, and the Lord has not sent them, yet they expect their word to be fulfilled.
\v 7 Have you not seen a falsehood? And spoken empty prophecies? 
\v 8 Therefore say, 
\p Thus says the Lord; Because your words are false, and your prophecies are empty, therefore, behold, I am against you, says the Lord. 
\v 9 I will stretch forth my hand against the prophets that see falsehoods, and those who utter vanities: they will not partake of the instruction of my people, neither they will be written in the roll of the house of Israel, and they will not enter into the land of Israel; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\v 10 Because they have caused my people to err, saying, Peace, peace; and there is no peace; and one builds a wall, and they plaster it, as if it might fall. 
\p
\v 11 Say to those who plaster, It will fall; and there will be a flooding rain; and I will send great stones upon their joinings, and they will fall; and there will be a sweeping wind, and it will be broken. 
\v 12 Lo! The wall has fallen; and will they not say to you, Where is your plaster with which you plastered \add it\add*? 
\v 13 Therefore thus says the Lord; I will even cause a sweeping blast to burst forth with fury, and there will be a flooding rain in my wrath; and in \add my\add* fury I will bring on great stones for complete destruction. 
\v 14 I will break down the wall which you have plastered, and it will fall; and I will lay it on the ground, and its foundations will be uncovered, and it will fall; and you will be consumed with rebukes: and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 I will accomplish my wrath upon the wall, and upon those who plaster it; it will fall: and I said to you, The wall is no more, nor those who plaster it, 
\v 16 even the prophets of Israel, who prophesy concerning Jerusalem, and who see \add visions of\add* peace for her, when there is no peace, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 17 You, son of man, set your face firmly against the daughters of your people who prophesy out of their own heart; and prophesy against them. 
\v 18 You will say, Thus says the Lord, Woe to the \add women\add* who sew bands for every arm, and make coverings for every head of every age in order to ensnare souls! The souls of my people have been ensnared, and they preserve souls for themselves. 
\v 19 They have dishonoured me before my people for a handful of barley, and for pieces of bread, to kill the souls which should not die, and to save alive the souls which should not live, while you speak to a people hearing vain speeches. 
\p
\v 20 Therefore thus says the Lord God, Behold, I am against your arm bands, by which you confound souls there, and I will tear them away from your arms, and will set at liberty their souls which you pervert to scatter them. 
\v 21 I will tear your head-coverings, and will rescue my people out of your hand, and they will no longer be in your hands to be greatly agitated; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 22 Because you have ensnared the heart of the righteous, because I didn't ensnare him, and \add that\add* in order to strengthen the hands of the wicked, that he should not at all turn from his evil way and live: 
\v 23 therefore you will surely not see falsehoods and you will surely not utter prophecies any more: but I will deliver my people out of your hand; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 14 
\p
\v 1 Men of the people of Israel came to me from the elders, and sat before me. 
\v 2 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 3 Son of man, these men have conceived their plans in their hearts, and have set the consequence of their wicked deeds before their face: will I indeed answer them? 
\v 4 Therefore speak to them, and you will say to them, Thus says the Lord; Any man of the house of Israel, who will conceive his plans in his heart, and will set the consequence of his wickedness before his face, and will come to the prophet; I the Lord will answer him \add according to the things\add* in which his mind is entangled, 
\v 5 that he should turn aside the house of Israel, according to their hearts that are estranged from me in their thoughts. 
\p
\v 6 Therefore say to the house of Israel, Thus says the Lord God, Be converted, and turn from your \add evil\add* practices, and from all your sins, and turn your faces back again. 
\v 7 For any man of the house of Israel, or of the strangers that sojourn in Israel, who will separate himself from me, and conceive his imaginations in his heart, and set before his face the consequence of his wickedness, and come to the prophet to enquire of him concerning me; I the Lord will answer him, \add according to the things\add* wherein he is entangled. 
\v 8 I will set my face against that man, and will make him desolate and ruined, and will cut him off from the midst of my people; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 9 If a prophet is led astray and speaks, I the Lord have led that prophet astray, and will stretch out my hand against him, and will destroy him from the midst of my people Israel. 
\v 10 They will bear their guilt: the guilt of the one who asks will be the same as the guilt of the prophet
\v 11 that the house of Israel may no more go astray from me, and so they may no more defile themselves with any of their transgressions: so they will be my people, and I will be their God, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 12 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 13 Son of man, if a land will sin against me by committing a trespass, then will I stretch out my hand upon it, and will break its staff of bread, and will send forth famine upon it, and cut off from it man and beast. 
\v 14 Though these three men should be among it, Noah, and \f + \fr 14:14 \ft Daniel here likely refers to an ancient figure (Danel) known for righteousness, not the biblical Daniel.\f*Daniel, and Job, they \add alone\add* should be delivered by their righteousness, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 If again I bring evil beasts upon the land, and take vengeance upon it, and it be ruined, and there be no one to pass through for fear of the wild beasts: 
\v 16 and \add if\add* these three men should be among it, \add as\add* I live, says the Lord, neither sons nor daughters will be saved, but these only will be saved, and the land will be destroyed. 
\v 17 Or again if I bring a sword upon that land, and say, Let the sword go through the land; and I cut off from them man and beast: 
\v 18 though these three men were among it, as I live, says the Lord, they will not deliver sons or daughters, but they only will be saved themselves. 
\p
\v 19 Or \add if\add* again I send pestilence upon that land, and pour out my wrath upon it in blood, to destroy from off it man and beast: 
\v 20 and should Noah, and \f + \fr 14:20 \ft See previous note.\f*Daniel, and Job, be among it, \add as\add* I live, says the Lord, there will be left \add them\add* neither sons nor daughters; \add only\add* they by their righteousness will deliver their souls. 
\p
\v 21 Thus says the Lord, And if I even send upon Jerusalem my four severe punishments, sword, and famine, and evil beasts, and pestilence, to destroy from out of it man and beast; 
\v 22 yet, behold, \add there will be\add* men left in it, those who escaped it, who \add will\add* lead forth sons and daughters from it: behold, they \add will\add* go forth to you, and you will see their ways and their thoughts: and you will mourn over the evils which I have brought upon Jerusalem, \add even\add* all the evils which I have brought upon it. 
\v 23 They will comfort you, because you will see their ways and their thoughts: and you will know that I have not done in vain all that I have done in it, says the Lord. 
\c 15 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 2 You, son of man—of all the wood of the branches that are among the trees of the forest, what will be made of the wood of the vine? 
\v 3 Will they take wood from it to make \add it fit\add* for work? Will they take from it a peg to hang any vessel upon it? 
\v 4 It is only given to the fire to be consumed; the fire consumes that which is yearly pruned of it, and it is completely gone. Will it be useful for \add any\add* work? 
\v 5 Not even while it is still whole will it be \add useful\add* for \add any\add* work: if the fire will have completely consumed it, will it still be \add fit\add* for work? 
\v 6 Therefore say, 
\p Thus says the Lord, As the vine-tree among the trees of the forest, which I have given up to the fire to be consumed, so have I given up the inhabitants of Jerusalem. 
\v 7 I will set my face against them; they will go forth from the fire, and \add yet\add* fire will devour them; and they will know that I am the Lord, when I have set my face against them. 
\v 8 I will give up the land to ruin, because they have completely transgressed, says the Lord. 
\c 16 
\p
\v 1 Moreover the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, testify to Jerusalem \add of\add* her iniquities; 
\v 3 and you will say, 
\p Thus says the Lord to Jerusalem; Your root and your birth are of the land of Canaan: your father was an Amorite, and your mother a Hittite. 
\v 4 And \add as for\add* your birth in the day wherein you were born, you did not bind your \f + \fr 16:4 \fqa Gr. \ft μαστούς 'breasts'.\f*umbilical cord, and you were not washed in water, nor were you salted with salt, nor were you swathed in swaddling-bands. 
\v 5 Nor did my eye pity you, to do any of these things for you, to show you any compassion; but you were cast out on the face of the field, \f + \fr 16:5 \fqa Gr. \ft because of the crookedness of your soul. This reflects a Hebrew idiom signifying rejection.\f*because you were loathed, in the day when you were born. 
\p
\v 6 I passed by to you, and saw you covered in your blood; and I said to you, \f + \fr 16:6 \fqa Gr. \ft Life out of your blood.\f*Live!
\v 7 Increase! I have made you as the springing grass of the field. So you increased and grew, and you \f+ \fr 16:7 \fqa Gr. \ft entered a city of cities.\f*came to maturity: your breasts were formed, and your hair grew, yet you were naked and bare. 
\p
\v 8 I passed by you and saw you, and, behold, your time was the time for love; and I spread my wings over you, and covered your nakedness, and swore to you: and I entered into covenant with you, says the Lord, and you became mine. 
\v 9 I washed you in water, and washed your blood from you, and anointed you with oil. 
\v 10 I clothed you with embroidered \add garments\add*, and clothed you beneath with purple, and girded you with fine linen, and clothed you with silk, 
\v 11 and decked you also with ornaments, and put bracelets on your hands, and a necklace on your neck. 
\v 12 I put a ring on your nose, and earrings in your ears, and a crown of glory on your head. 
\v 13 So you were adorned with gold and silver; and your clothing was of fine linen, and silk, and variegated work: you ate fine flour, and oil, and honey, and became extremely beautiful. 
\v 14 Your name went out among the nations for your beauty: because it was perfected with elegance, \add and\add* in the comeliness which I put upon you, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 You trusted in your beauty, and played the prostitute because of your renown, and poured out your prostitution on every passer by. 
\v 16 You took of your garments, and made to yourself idols of needlework, and played the prostitute with them; such a thing shall surely not happen, it shall surely not be.
\v 17 You took your fair ornaments of my gold and of my silver, of what I gave you, and you made to yourself male images, and you committed prostitution with them. 
\v 18 You took your variegated clothing and clothed them, and you set before them my oil and my incense. 
\v 19 And \add you took\add* my bread which I gave you, (\add yes\add* I fed you with fine flour and oil and honey) and set it before them for a sweet-smelling savour: yes, it was so, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 20 You took your sons and your daughters, whom you bore, and sacrificed \add these\add* to them to be destroyed. You played the prostitute as \add if that were\add* little, 
\v 21 and killed your children, and gave them up, using them in your abominations.
\v 22 This is beyond all your prostitution, and you did not remember your infancy, when you were naked and bare, \add and\add* lived \add though\add* covered in your blood. 
\p
\v 23 It happened after all your wickedness, says the Lord, 
\v 24 that you built yourself a house of prostitution, and made yourself a public place in every street; 
\v 25 and at every street corner you set up your places of prostitution, and defiled your beauty, and spread your legs to every passer by, and multiplied your prostitution. 
\v 26 You prostituted yourself with your neighbours the well-endowed sons of Egypt; and you multiplied your prostitution to provoke me. 
\p
\v 27 If I stretch out my hand against you, then will I abolish your statutes, and deliver \add you\add* up to the wills of those who hate you, \add even to\add* the daughters of the Philistines that turned you aside from the way in which you sinned. 
\p
\v 28 You prostituted yourself to the daughters of Assur, and you were not even satisfied with this; yes, you prostituted yourself and were not satisfied. 
\v 29 You multiplied your covenants with the land of the Chaldeans; and not even with these were you satisfied. 
\p
\v 30 What am I to do with \f + \fr 16:30 \fqa Gr. \ft your daughter.\f*you, says the Lord, when you have done all these things, the works of a prostitute? And you prostited yourself again and again and again.
\v 31 Throughout your \f + \fr 16:31 \fqa Gr. \ft daughters\f*towns you built your places of prostitution on every street corner, and have set up your platform in every square; and you did become like a prostitute collecting payment.
\v 32 You are like an adulterous woman who receives payment from her husband. 
\v 33 She gave payment to all who came to her; and you have given payment to all your lovers, yes, you even paid them to come to you from all around for your prostitution. 
\p
\v 34 And your prostitution became perverse beyond that of \add other\add* women: they prostituted themselves with you while you gave payment, and no payments were given to you; and so you became perverse.
\p
\v 35 Therefore, prostitute, hear the word of the Lord: 
\v 36 Thus says the Lord, Because you have poured forth your money, therefore your shame will be uncovered in your prostitution with your lovers, and \add with\add* regard to all the imaginations of your iniquities, and for the blood of your children which you have given to them. 
\v 37 Therefore, behold, I \add will\add* gather all your lovers with whom you have consorted, and all whom you have loved, with all whom you hated; and I will gather them against you all around, and will expose your wickedness to them, and they will see all your shame. 
\v 38 I will be avenged on you with the vengeance of an adulteress, and I will bring upon you blood of fury and zeal. 
\v 39 I will deliver you into their hands, and they will break down your place of prostitution, and destroy your platforms; and they will strip you of your garments, and will take your proud ornaments, and leave you naked and bare. 
\v 40 They will bring multitudes upon you, and they will stone you with stones, and pierce you with their swords. 
\v 41 They will burn your houses with fire, and will execute vengeance on you in the sight of many women: and I will turn you back from prostitution, and I will not give rewards any more.
\p
\v 42 So I will pour out my wrath upon you, and my jealousy will depart from you, and I will be at rest, and will no longer be concerned.
\v 43 Because you did not remember your infancy, and you grieved me in all these things; therefore, behold, I have repayed your ways upon your head, says the Lord: for thus you have worked ungodliness above all your \add other\add* iniquities. 
\p
\v 44 These are all the things they have spoken against you in a proverb, saying, Like mother, like daughter.
\v 45 You are your mother's daughter, who rejected her husband and her children; and you are the sister of your sisters who rejected their husbands and their children: your mother was a Hittite, and \add your\add* father an Amorite. 
\v 46 Your elder sister who dwells on your left hand is Samaria, she and her daughters: and your younger sister, that dwells on your right hand, is Sodom and her daughters. 
\v 47 Yet you have not walked in their ways, or act according to their iniquities; before long you surpassed them in all your ways. 
\p
\v 48 \add As\add* I live, says the Lord, Sodom, your sister, she and her daughters have not done as you and your daughters have done. 
\v 49 Now this was the sin of your sister Sodom: pride, fulness of bread and prosperous ease; she and her daughters lived in luxury. This was hers and her daughters': they did not strengthen the hand of the poor.
\v 50 They boasted, and worked iniquities before me: so I cut them off as I saw \add fit\add*. 
\p
\v 51 Also Samaria has not sinned according to half of your sins; but you have multiplied your iniquities beyond them, and you have justified your sisters in all your iniquities which you have committed. 
\v 52 You therefore bear your punishment, for that you have corrupted your sisters by your sins which you have committed beyond them; and you have made them \add appear\add* more righteous than yourself: therefore be ashamed, and bear your dishonour, in that you have justified your sisters. 
\v 53 I will turn their captivity, \add even\add* the captivity of Sodom and her daughters; and I will turn the captivity of Samaria and her daughters; and I will turn your captivity among them: 
\v 54 that you may bear your punishment, and be put to shame for all that you have done by provoking me to anger. 
\p
\v 55 Your sister Sodom and her daughters will be restored as they were at the beginning, and you and your daughters will be restored as you were at the beginning. 
\p
\v 56 Surely your sister Sodom was not mentioned by your mouth in the days of your pride: 
\v 57 before your wickedness was uncovered, even now you are the reproach of the daughters of Syria, and of all that are all around her, \add even\add* of the daughters of the Philistines that surround you.
\v 58 \add As for\add* your ungodliness and your iniquities, you have borne them, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 59 Thus says the Lord; I will even do to you as you have done, as you have dealt shamefully in these things to transgress my covenant. 
\v 60 I will remember my covenant \add made\add* with you in the days of your infancy, and I will establish to you an everlasting covenant. 
\v 61 Then you will remember your way, and will be completely dishonoured when you receive your elder sisters with your younger ones: and I will give them to you for building up, but not by your covenant. 
\v 62 I will establish my covenant with you; and you will know that I am the Lord: 
\v 63 that you may remember, and be ashamed, and may no more be able to open your mouth for your shame, when I am reconciled to you for all that you have done, says the Lord. 
\c 17 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, relate a tale, and speak a parable to the house of Israel: 
\v 3 and you will say, Thus says the Lord; 
\p A great eagle, great-winged, long in span, full of talons, with the power to enter Lebanon, took the choice \add branches\add* of the cedar: 
\v 4 he plucked off the tops of the tender shoots, and brought them into the land of Canaan; he set them in a city of merchants. 
\v 5 He took some of the seed of the land, and planted it in a field; he placed it by abundant water; setting it carefully.
\v 6 It sprouted, and became a low spreading vine, small in height; its branches turned towards him, and its roots remained under it. So it became a vine, and produced shoots, and sent out its tendrils. 
\p
\v 7 There was another great eagle, great-winged and full of talons: and, behold, this vine bent itself toward him, and its roots \add turned\add* towards him, and it sent out its branches towards him, so \add he\add* might water it from the bed where it was planted.
\v 8 It had been plnated in a good field by abundant waters, so that it might produce brances and bear fruit and become a splendid vine. 
\p
\v 9 Therefore say, Thus says the Lord; Will it prosper? Will he not pull up its roots and cut off its fruit so that it withers, so that all its fresh growth dries up? It will not take a strong arm or many people to pull it up by its roots. 
\v 10 And, behold, though it is planted, will it prosper? Will it not utterly wither as soon as the east wind touches it? It wither on the bed where it sprouted.
\p
\v 11 Moreover the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 12 Son of man, say now to the rebellious house, Don't you know what these things were? Say \add to them\add*, Whenever the king of Babylon will come against Jerusalem, then he will take her king and her princes, and will take them home to Babylon. 
\v 13 He will take of the royal seed, and will make a covenant with him, and will bind him with an oath: and he will take the princes of the land: 
\v 14 that it may become a weak kingdom, so as never to lift itself up, that he may keep his covenant, and establish it. 
\v 15 And \add if\add* he will revolt from him, to send his messengers into Egypt, that \add they\add* may give him horses and much people; will he prosper? Will he who acts as an adversary be preserved? And will he who transgresses the covenant be preserved? 
\p
\v 16 \add As\add* I live, says the Lord, truly in \add the same\add* place where the king is who made him king, who dishonoured my oath, and who broke my covenant, he will die with him among Babylon. 
\v 17 Pharaoh will not make war against him with a large force or great multitude, in throwing up a mound, and in building of siege towers, to destroy many lives.
\v 18 Because he has profaned the oath so as to break the covenant, when, behold, I engaged his hand, and he has done all these things to him, he will not escape. 
\p
\v 19 Therefore say, Thus says the Lord; \add As\add* I live, surely my oath which he has profaned, and my covenant which he has transgressed, I will even repay it upon his head. 
\v 20 I will spread a net upon him, and he will be caught in its snare. 
\v 21 In every battle of his they will fall by the sword, and I will scatter \add his\add* remnant to every wind: and you will know that I the Lord have spoken it. 
\p
\v 22 For thus says the Lord; I will even take of the choice \add branches\add* of the cedar from the top \add of it\add*, I will crop off their hearts, and I will plant it on a high mountain: 
\v 23 and I will hang it on a lofty mountain of Israel: yes, I will plant it, and it will put forth shoots, and will bear fruit, and it will be a great cedar: and every bird will rest beneath it, even every fowl will rest under its shadow: its branches will be restored. 
\v 24 All the trees of the field will know that I am the Lord who bring low the high tree, and exalt the low tree, and wither the green tree, and cause the dry tree to flourish: I the Lord have spoken, and will do \add it\add*. 
\c 18 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, what do you mean by this parable among the children of Israel, saying, The fathers have eaten unripe grapes, and the children's teeth have been set on edge? 
\p
\v 3 \add As\add* I live, says the Lord, surely this parable will no more be spoken in Israel. 
\v 4 For all souls are mine; as the soul of the father, so also the soul of the son, they are mine: the soul that sins, it will die. 
\p
\v 5 But the man who will be just, who executes judgment and righteousness, 
\v 6 who will not eat upon the mountains, and will not at all lift up his eyes to the intentions of the house of Israel, and will not defile his neighbour's wife, and will not approach a woman during her period,
\v 7 and will not oppress any man, \add but\add* will return the pledge of the debtor, and will be guilty of no plunder, will give his bread to the hungry, and clothe the naked; 
\v 8 and will not lend his money upon usury, and will not receive usurious increase, and will turn back his hand from injustice, will execute righteous judgment between a man and his neighbour, 
\v 9 and has walked in my commandments and kept my ordinances, to do them; he is righteous, he will surely live, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 10 If he beget a mischievous son, shedding blood and committing sins, 
\v 11 who has not walked in the way of his righteous father, but has even eaten upon the mountains, and has defiled his neighbour's wife, 
\v 12 and has oppressed the poor and needy, and has committed robbery, and not restored a pledge, and has set his eyes upon idols, has worked iniquities, 
\v 13 has lent upon usury, and taken usurious increase; he will by no means live: he has worked all these iniquities; he will surely die; his blood will be upon him. 
\p
\v 14 If he beget a son, and \add the son\add* sees all his father's sins which he has worked, and fears, and does not do according to them, 
\v 15 and \add if he\add* has not eaten on the mountains, and has not set his eyes on the intentions of the house of Israel, and has not defiled his neighbour's wife, 
\v 16 and has not oppressed a man, and has not retained the pledge, nor committed robbery, has given his bread to the hungry, and has clothed the naked, 
\v 17 and has turned back his hand from unrighteousness, has not received interest or usurious increase, has worked righteousness, and walked in my ordinances; he will not die for the iniquities of his father, he will surely live. 
\v 18 But if his father grievously afflict, or plunder, he has acted wickedly among my people, and will die in his wickedness. 
\p
\v 19 But you will say, Why has the son not borne the wickedness of the father? Because the son has worked judgment and mercy, has kept all my statutes, and done them, he will surely live. 
\v 20 But the soul that sins will die: and the son will not bear the wickedness of the father, nor will the father bear the wickedness of the son: the righteousness of the righteous will be upon him, and the wickedness of the transgressor will be upon him. 
\p
\v 21 If the transgressor turn away from all his iniquities which he has committed, and keep all my commandments, and do justice and mercy, he will surely live, and will by no means die. 
\v 22 None of his trespasses which he has committed will be remembered: in his righteousness which he has done he will live. 
\v 23 Will I at all desire the death of the sinner, says the Lord, as I \add desire\add* that he should turn from \add his\add* evil way, and live? 
\p
\v 24 But when the righteous man turns away from his righteousness, and commits wickedness, according to all the transgressions which the transgressor has worked, none of his righteousness which he has worked will be at all remembered: in his trespass in which he has trespassed, and in his sins in which he has sinned, in them he will die. 
\p
\v 25 Yet you have said, The way of the Lord isn't straight. Hear now, all the house of Israel; will not my way be straight? Is your way straight? 
\v 26 When the righteous turns away from his righteousness and commits a trespass, and dies in the trespass which he has committed, he will \add even\add* die in it. 
\v 27 When the wicked man turns away from his wickedness that he has committed, and will do judgment and justice, he has kept his soul, 
\v 28 and has turned away from all his ungodliness which he has committed: he will surely live, he will not die. 
\p
\v 29 Yet the house of Israel say, The way of the Lord isn't right. Isn't my way right, O house of Israel? Isn't your way wrong? 
\v 30 I will judge you, O house of Israel, says the Lord, each one according to his way: be converted, and turn from all your ungodliness, and it will not become to you the punishment of wickedness. 
\v 31 Cast away from yourselves all your ungodliness wherein you have sinned against me; and make to yourselves a new heart and a new spirit: for why should you die, O house of Israel? 
\v 32 For I don't desire the death of him who dies, says the Lord. 
\c 19 
\p
\v 1 Moreover, take up a lamentation for the prince of Israel, 
\v 2 and say, Why has your mother become a cub among lions? Among lions she has multiplied her whelps. 
\v 3 One of her whelps sprang forth; he became a lion, and learned to take prey, he devoured men. 
\v 4 The nations heard a report of him; he was caught in their pit, and they brought him into the land of Egypt in chains. 
\p
\v 5 She saw that he was driven away from her, \add and\add* her hope \add of him\add* perished, and she took another of her whelps; she made him a lion. 
\v 6 He went up and down among lions, he became a lion, and learned to take prey, he devoured men. 
\v 7 He prowled in his boldness and laid waste their cities, and made the land desolate, and the fulness of it, by the voice of his roaring. 
\p
\v 8 Then the nations set upon him from the lands all around, and they spread their nets upon him: he was taken in their pit. 
\v 9 They put him in chains and in a cage, \add and\add* he came to the king of Babylon; and he cast him into prison, that his voice should not be heard on the mountains of Israel. 
\p
\v 10 Your mother was as a vine and as a blossom on a pomegranate tree, planted by water: her fruit and her shoots abounded because of much water. 
\v 11 She became a rod for a tribe of princes, and was elevated in her bulk among \add other\add* trees, and she saw her bulk in the multitude of her branches. 
\p
\v 12 But she was broken down in wrath, she was cast upon the ground, and the east wind dried up her choice \add branches\add*: vengeance came upon them, and the rod of her strength was withered; fire consumed it. 
\v 13 Now they have planted her in the wilderness, in a dry land. 
\v 14 Fire has gone out of a rod of her choice \add boughs\add*, and has devoured her; and there was no rod of strength in her. Her race has become a parable of lamentation, and it will be for a lamentation. 
\c 20 
\p
\v 1 It happened in the seventh year, on the fifteenth day of the month, men of the elders of the house of Israel came to enquire of the Lord, and they sat before me. 
\v 2 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 3 Son of man, speak to the elders of the house of Israel, and you will say to them, Thus says the Lord; Have you come to enquire of me? \add As\add* I live, I will not be enquired of by you, says the Lord. 
\v 4 Will I completely take vengeance on them, son of man? Testify to them of the iniquities of their fathers: 
\v 5 and you will say to them, Thus says the Lord; 
\p From the day that I chose the house of Israel, and became known to the seed of the house of Jacob, and was known to them in the land of Egypt, and helped them with my hand, saying, I am the Lord your God; 
\v 6 in that day I helped them with my hand, to bring them out of the land of Egypt into the land which I prepared for them, a land flowing with milk and honey, it is abundant beyond every land. 
\v 7 I said to them, Let every one cast away the abominations of his eyes, and don't defile yourselves with the devices of Egypt: I am the Lord your God. 
\p
\v 8 But they revolted from me, and would not listen to me: they didn't cast away the abominations of their eyes, and didn't forsake the devices of Egypt: then I said that I would pour out my wrath upon them, to accomplish my wrath upon them among Egypt. 
\v 9 But I worked \add so\add* that my name should surely not be profaned in the sight of the nations, among whom they are, among whom I was made known to them in their sight, to bring them out of the land of Egypt. 
\p
\v 10 I brought them into the wilderness. 
\v 11 I gave them my commandments, and made known to them my ordinances, all which \add if\add* a man will do, he will even live in them. 
\v 12 I gave them my sabbaths, that they should be for a sign between me and them, that they should know that I am the Lord who sanctify them. 
\p
\v 13 I said to the house of Israel in the wilderness, Walk in my commandments: but they didn't walk \add in them\add*, and they rejected my ordinances, which \add if\add* a man will do, he will even live in them; and they grievously profaned my sabbaths: and I said that I would pour out my wrath upon them in the wilderness, to consume them. 
\v 14 But I worked \add so\add* that my name should surely not be profaned before the nations, before whose eyes I brought them out. 
\p
\v 15 But I lifted up my hand against them in the wilderness once for all, that I would not bring them into the land which I gave them, a land flowing with milk and honey, it is sweeter than all lands: 
\v 16 because they rejected my ordinances, and didn't walk in my commandments, but profaned my sabbaths, and went after the imaginations of their hearts. 
\p
\v 17 Yet my eyes spared them, so as \add not\add* to destroy them completely, and I did not make an end of them in the wilderness. 
\v 18 I said to their children in the wilderness, Don't walk in the customs of your fathers, and don't keep their ordinances, and have no fellowship with their practices, nor defile yourselves \add with them\add*. 
\v 19 I \add am\add* the Lord your God; walk in my commandments, and keep my ordinances, and do them; 
\v 20 and make my sabbaths holy, and let them be a sign between me and you, that you may know that I am the Lord your God. 
\p
\v 21 But they provoked me, and their children didn't walk in my commandments, and they took no heed to my ordinances to do them, which \add if\add* a man will do, he will even live in them, and they profaned my sabbaths: then I said that I would pour out my wrath upon them in the wilderness, to accomplish my anger upon them. 
\v 22 But I worked so that my name might surely not be profaned before the nations; and I brought them out in their sight. 
\p
\v 23 I lifted up my hand against them in the wilderness, that I would scatter them among the nations, \add and\add* disperse them in the lands; 
\v 24 because they didn't keep my ordinances, and rejected my commandments, and profaned my sabbaths, and their eyes went after the imaginations of their fathers. 
\p
\v 25 So I gave them commandments \add that were\add* not good, and ordinances in which they should not live. 
\v 26 I will defile them by their \add own\add* decrees, when I pass through upon every one that opens the womb, that I may destroy them. 
\p
\v 27 Therefore, son of man, speak to the house of Israel, and you will say to them, Thus says the Lord: Your fathers have provoked me here in their trespasses in which they transgressed against me. 
\v 28 Because I brought them into the land concerning which I lifted up my hand to give them; and they looked upon every high hill, and every shady tree, and they sacrificed there to their gods, and offered there a sweet-smelling savour, and there they poured out their drink-offerings. 
\v 29 I said to them, What is Abama, that you go in there? And they called its name Abama, until this day. 
\p
\v 30 Therefore say to the house of Israel, Thus says the Lord, Do you pollute yourselves with the iniquities of your fathers, and do you go playing the prostitute after their abominations, 
\v 31 and \add do you pollute yourselves\add* with the first-fruits of your gifts, in the offerings with which you pollute yourselves in all your imaginations, until this day; and will I answer you, O house of Israel? \add As\add* I live, says the Lord, I will not answer you, neither will this thing come upon your spirit. 
\v 32 It will not be as you say, We will be as the nations, and as the tribes of the earth, to worship wood and stone. 
\p
\v 33 Therefore, \add as\add* I live, says the Lord, I will reign over you with a strong hand, and with a high arm, and with outpoured wrath: 
\v 34 I will bring you out from the nations, and will take you out of the lands in which you were dispersed, with a strong hand, and with a high arm, and with outpoured wrath. 
\v 35 I will bring you into the wilderness of the nations, and will plead with you there face to face. 
\p
\v 36 As I pleaded with your fathers in the wilderness of the land of Egypt, so will I judge you, says the Lord. 
\v 37 I will cause you to pass under my rod, and I will bring you in by number. 
\v 38 I will separate from among you the ungodly and the revolters; for I will lead them forth out of their place of sojourning, and they will not enter into the land of Israel: and you will know that I am the Lord, \add even\add* the Lord. 
\p
\v 39 And \add as to\add* you, O house of Israel, thus says the Lord, \add even\add* the Lord; Put away each one his \add evil\add* practices, and hereafter if you listen to me, then you will no more profane my holy name by your gifts and by devices. 
\v 40 For upon my holy mountain, on the high mountain, says the Lord, \add even\add* the Lord, there will all the house of Israel serve me forever: and there will I accept \add you\add*, and there will I have respect to your first-fruits, and the first-fruits of your offerings, in all your holy things. 
\p
\v 41 I will accept you with a sweet-smelling savour, when I bring you out from the nations, and take you out of the lands wherein you have been dispersed; and I will be sanctified among you in the sight of the nations. 
\v 42 You will know that I am the Lord, when I have brought you into the land of Israel, into the land concerning which I lifted up my hand to give it to your fathers. 
\v 43 You will there remember your ways, and your devices with which you defiled yourselves; and you will bewail yourselves for all your wickedness. 
\v 44 You will know that I am the Lord, when I have done thus to you, that my name may not be profaned in your evil ways, and in your corrupt devices, says the Lord. 
\c 21 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, set your face against Thæman, and look toward Darom, and prophesy against the chief forest of Nageb, 
\v 3 and you will say to the forest of Nageb, Hear the word of the Lord; thus says the Lord, \add even\add* the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* kindle a fire in you, and it will devour in you every green tree, and every dry tree: the flame that is kindled will not be quenched, and every face will be scorched with it from the south to the north. 
\v 4 All flesh will know that I the Lord have kindled it: it will not be quenched. 
\p
\v 5 I said, Not so, O Lord God! They say to me, Isn't this that is spoken a parable? 
\p
\v 6 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 7 Therefore prophesy, son of man, set your face steadfastly toward Jerusalem, and look toward their holy places, and you will prophesy against the land of Israel, 
\v 8 and you will say to the land of Israel, Thus says the Lord; Behold, I am against you, and I will draw forth my sword out of its sheath, and I will destroy out of you the transgressor and unrighteous. 
\v 9 Because I will destroy out of you the unrighteous and the transgressor, \add therefore\add* so will my sword come forth out of its sheath against all flesh from the south to the north: 
\v 10 and all flesh will know that I the Lord have drawn forth my sword out of its sheath: it will not return any more. 
\p
\v 11 You, son of man, groan with the breaking of your loins; you will even groan heavily in their sight. 
\v 12 It will come to pass, if they will say to you, Why do you groan? That you will say, For the report; because it comes: and every heart will break, and all hands will become feeble, and all flesh and every spirit will faint, and all thighs will be defiled with moisture: behold, it comes, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 13 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 14 Son of man, prophesy, and you will say, Thus says the Lord; Say, Sword, sword, be sharpened and rage, 
\v 15 that you may kill victims; be sharpened that you may be bright, ready for slaughter, kill, despise, despise every tree. 
\v 16 He made it ready for his hand to hold: the sword is sharpened, it is ready to put into the hand of the slayer. 
\p
\v 17 Cry out and howl, son of man: for this \add sword\add* has come upon my people, this \add sword has come\add* upon all the princes of Israel: they will be as strangers: \add judgment\add* with the sword has come upon my people: therefore clap your hands, for sentence has been passed: 
\v 18 and what if even the tribe is rejected? It will not be, says the Lord God. 
\p
\v 19 You, son of man, prophesy, and clap your hands, and take a second sword: the third sword is \add the sword\add* of the killed, the great sword of the killed: and you will strike them with amazement, lest the heart should faint 
\v 20 and the weak ones be multiplied at every gate—they are given up to the slaughter of the sword: it is well fitted for slaughter, it is well fitted for glittering. 
\v 21 Go on, sharpen yourself on the right and on the left wherever your face may set itself. 
\p
\v 22 I also will clap my hands, and let loose my fury: I the Lord have spoken \add it\add*. 
\p
\v 23 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 24 You, son of man, appoint yourself two ways, that the sword of the king of Babylon may enter in: the two will go forth from one country; and \add there will be\add* a force at the top of the way of the city, you will set \add it\add* at the top of the way, 
\v 25 that the sword may enter in upon Rabbath of the children of Ammon, and upon Judea, and upon Jerusalem in the midst of it. 
\p
\v 26 For the king of Babylon will stand on the old way, at the head of the two ways, to use divination, to make bright the arrow, and to enquire of the graven images, and to examine \add the victims\add*. 
\v 27 On his right was the divination against Jerusalem, to cast a mound, to open the mouth in shouting, to lift up the voice with crying, to cast a mound against her gates, to cast up a heap, and to build siege-towers. 
\v 28 He was to them as one using divination before them, and he himself recounting his iniquities, that they might be borne in mind. 
\p
\v 29 Therefore thus says the Lord, Because you have caused your iniquities to be remembered, in the discovery of your wickedness, so that your sins should be seen, in all your wickedness and in your \add evil\add* practices; because you have caused remembrance \add of them\add*, in these will you be taken. 
\v 30 You profane wicked prince of Israel, whose day, \add even\add* an end, has come in a season of wickedness, thus says the Lord; 
\v 31 You have taken off the mitre and put on the crown, it will not have such \add another\add* after it: you have abased that which was high, and exalted that which was low. 
\v 32 Injustice, injustice, injustice, I will make it: woe to it: such will it be until he comes to whom it belongs; and I will deliver \add it\add* to him. 
\p
\v 33 You, son of man, prophesy, and you will say, Thus says the Lord, concerning the children of Ammon, and concerning their reproach; and you will say, O sword, sword, drawn for slaughter, and drawn for destruction, awake, that you may gleam. 
\v 34 While you are seeing vain \add visions\add*, and while you are prophesying lies, to bring yourself upon the necks of ungodly transgressors, the day has come, \add even\add* an end, in a season of wickedness. 
\p
\v 35 Turn, don't rest in this place in which you were born: in your own land will I judge you. 
\v 36 I will pour out my wrath upon you, I will blow upon you with the fire of my wrath, and I will deliver you into the hands of barbarians skilled in working destruction. 
\v 37 You will be fuel for fire; your blood will be among your land; there will be no remembrance at all of you: for I the Lord have spoken \add it\add*. 
\c 22 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 You, son of man, will you judge the bloody city? Yes, declare you to her all her iniquities. 
\v 3 You will say, Thus says the Lord God: O city that sheds blood within her, so that her time should come, and that forms plans against herself, to defile herself; 
\v 4 in their blood which you have shed, you have transgressed; and in your intentions which you have formed, you have polluted yourself; and you have brought near your days, and have brought on the time of your years: therefore have I made you a reproach to the nations, and a mockery to all the lands, 
\v 5 to those near you, and to those far distant from you; and they will mock you, \add you who are\add* notoriously unclean, and abundant in iniquities. 
\p
\v 6 Behold, the princes of the house of Israel have conspired in you each one with his relatives, that they might shed blood. 
\v 7 In you they have reviled father and mother; and in you they have behaved unjustly toward the stranger: they have oppressed the orphan and widow. 
\v 8 They have despise my holy things, and in you they have profaned my sabbaths. 
\v 9 \add There are\add* robbers in you, to shed blood in you; and in you they have eaten upon the mountains: they have worked ungodliness among you. 
\v 10 In you they have uncovered the father's nakedness; and in you they have violated a woman in her impurity. 
\v 11 They have dealt unlawfully each one with his neighbour's wife; and each one in ungodliness has defiled his daughter-in-law: and in you they have humbled each one his sister, the daughter of his father. 
\p
\v 12 In you they have received gifts to shed blood; they have received in you interest and usurious increase; and by oppression you have brought your wickedness to the full, and have forgotten me, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 13 If I will strike my hand at \add your iniquities\add* which you have accomplished, which you have worked, and at your blood that has been shed among you, 
\v 14 will your heart endure? Will your hands be strong in the days which I bring upon you? I the Lord have spoken, and will do \add it\add*. 
\v 15 I will scatter you among the nations, and disperse you in the lands, and your uncleanness will be removed from you. 
\v 16 I will take possession of you in the sight of the nations, and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 17 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 18 Son of man, behold, the house of Israel have all become to me \add as it were\add* mixed with brass, and iron, and tin, and lead; they are mixed up among silver. 
\p
\v 19 Therefore say, Thus says the Lord God; Because you have become one mixture, therefore I will gather you into the midst of Jerusalem. 
\v 20 As silver, and brass, and iron, and tin, and lead, are gathered into the midst of the furnace, to blow fire into it, so they may be melted: so will I take \add you\add* in my wrath, and I will gather and melt you. 
\v 21 I will blow upon you in the fire of my wrath, and you will be melted in the middle of it. 
\v 22 As silver is melted among a furnace, so will you be melted in the middle of it; and you will know that I the Lord have poured out my wrath upon you. 
\p
\v 23 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 24 Son of man, say to her, You are the land that isn't rained upon, neither has rain come upon you in the day of wrath: 
\v 25 whose princes among her are as roaring lions seizing prey, devouring souls by oppression, and taking bribes; and your widows are multiplied among you. 
\v 26 Her priests also have despise my law, and profaned my holy things: they have not distinguished between the holy and profane, nor have they distinguished between the unclean and the clean, and have hid their eyes from my sabbaths, and I was profaned among them. 
\v 27 Her princes among her are as wolves ravening to shed blood, so they may get dishonest gain. 
\v 28 Her prophets have whitewashed what is about to fall, who see vain things, who prophesy lies, saying, Thus says the Lord, when the Lord has not spoken,
\v 29 who sorely oppress the people of the land with injustice, and commit robbery; oppressing the poor and needy, and not dealing justly with the stranger. 
\p
\v 30 I sought from among them a man behaving uprightly, and standing before me perfectly in the time of wrath, so that I should not completely destroy her: but I didn't find \add him\add*. 
\v 31 So I have poured out my wrath on her in the fury of my anger, to accomplish \add it\add*. I have repayed their ways on their own heads, says the Lord God. 
\c 23 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, there were two women, daughters of one mother: 
\v 3 and they played the prostitute in Egypt in their youth: there their breasts fell, there they lost their virginity. 
\v 4 Their names were \f + \fr 23:4 \ft The names Ohola and Oholiba are transliterations from the Greek which in turn has transliterations of Hebrew words meaning ``her tent'' and ``my tent is in her'' respectively.\f*Ohola the elder, and Oholiba her sister: and they were mine, and bore sons and daughters: and \add as for\add* their names, Samaria was Ohola, and Jerusalem was Oholiba. 
\p
\v 5 Ohola played the prostitute from me, and doted on her lovers, on the Assyrians that were her neighbours, 
\v 6 clothed with purple, princes and captains; \add they were\add* young men and choice, all horsemen riding on horses. 
\v 7 She bestowed her prostitution upon them; all were choice sons of the Assyrians: and on whoever she doted herself, with them she defiled herself in all \add their\add* intentions. 
\v 8 She didn't forsake her prostitution with the Egyptians: for in her youth they committed prostitution with her, and they deflowered her, and poured out their prostitution upon her. 
\v 9 Therefore I delivered her into the hands of her lovers, into the hands of the children of the Assyrians, on whom she doted. 
\v 10 They uncovered her shame: they took her sons and daughters, and killed her with the sword: and she became a byword among women; and they worked vengeance in her for the sake of the daughters. 
\p
\v 11 Her sister Oholiba saw \add it\add*, and she indulged in her fondness more corruptly than she, and in her prostitution more than the prostitution of her sister. 
\v 12 She doted upon the sons of the Assyrians, princes and captains, her neighbours, clothed with fine linen, horsemen riding on horses; \add they were\add* all choice young men. 
\v 13 I saw that they were defiled, \add that\add* the two \add had\add* one way. 
\p
\v 14 She increased her prostitution, and she saw men painted on the wall, likenesses of the Chaldeans painted with a pencil, 
\v 15 having variegated girdles on their loins, having also richly dyed \add attire\add* upon their heads; all had a princely appearance, the likeness of the children of the Chaldeans, of their native land. 
\v 16 She doted upon them as soon as she saw them, and sent messengers to them into the land of the Chaldeans. 
\v 17 The sons of Babylon came to her, into the bed of rest, and they defiled her in her prostitution, and she was defiled by them, and her soul was alienated from them. 
\v 18 She exposed her prostitution, and exposed her shame: and my soul was alienated from her, even as my soul was alienated from her sister. 
\p
\v 19 You multiplied your prostitution, so as to call to remembrance the days of your youth, in which you committed whoredom in Egypt, 
\v 20 and you doted upon the Chaldeans, whose flesh is as the flesh of donkeys, and their members \add as\add* the members of horses. 
\v 21 You looked upon the wickedness of your youth, \add the things\add* which you wrought in Egypt in your lodging, where the breasts of your youth were. 
\p
\v 22 Therefore, Oholiba, thus says the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* stir up your lovers against you, from whom your soul is alienated, and I will bring them upon you all around, 
\v 23 the children of Babylon, and all the Chaldeans, Phacuc, and Sue, and Hychue, and all the sons of the Assyrians with them; choice young men, governors and captains, all princes and renowned, riding on horses. 
\v 24 They all will come upon you from the north, chariots and wheels, with a multitude of nations, shields and targets; and \add the enemy\add* will set a watch against you all around: and I will set judgment before them, and they will take vengeance on you with their judgments. 
\v 25 I will bring upon you my zeal, and they will deal with you in great wrath: they will cut off your nose and your ears; and will cast down your remnant with the sword: they will take your sons and your daughters; and fire will devour your remnant. 
\v 26 They will strip you of your clothing, and take \add away\add* your ornaments. 
\v 27 So I will turn back your ungodliness from you, and your prostitution from the land of Egypt: and you will not lift up your eyes upon them, and will no more remember Egypt. 
\p
\v 28 Therefore thus says the Lord God; Behold, I \add will\add* deliver you into the hands of those whom you hate, from whom your soul is alienated. 
\v 29 They will deal with you in hatred, and will take all \add the fruits\add* of your labours and your toils, and you will be naked and bare: and the shame of your prostitution will be exposed: and your ungodliness and your prostitution 
\v 30 brought this upon you, in that you played the prostitute after the nations, and defiled yourself with their devices. 
\p
\v 31 You walked in the way of your sister; and I will put her cup into your hands. 
\v 32 Thus says the Lord; Drink your sister's cup, deep and large, and full, to cause complete drunkenness. 
\v 33 You will be thoroughly weakened; and the cup of destruction, the cup of your sister Samaria, 
\v 34 drink it; and I will take away her feasts and her new moons: for I have spoken \add it\add*, says the Lord. 
\v 35 Therefore thus says the Lord; Because you have forgotten me, and cast me behind your back, therefore receive \add the reward\add* of your ungodliness and your prostitution. 
\p
\v 36 The Lord said to me; Son of man, will you not judge Ohola and Oholiba? And declare to them their iniquities? 
\v 37 For they have committed adultery, and blood was in their hands, even their intentions committed adultery, and they passed their children which they bore to me through the fire for them. 
\v 38 They even did this to me: they defiled my sanctuary, and profaned my sabbaths. 
\v 39 When they sacrificed their children to their idols, they also went into my sanctuary to profane it: and because they did this in my house; 
\v 40 and because they did this to the men who came from afar, to whom they sent messengers, and as soon as they came, immediately you washed yourself, and painted your eyes and adorned yourself with ornaments, 
\v 41 and sat on a prepared bed, and before it \add there was\add* a table set out, and \add as for\add* my incense and my oil, they rejoiced in them, 
\v 42 and they raised a sound of music, and \add that\add* with men coming from the wilderness out of a multitude of men, and they put bracelets on their hands, and a crown of glory on their heads; 
\p
\v 43 Therefore I said, Do they not commit adultery with these? And she has also done the deeds of a prostitute; she prostituted herself.
\v 44 They went in to her, as \add men\add* go in to a prostitute; so they went in to Ohola and to Oholiba to work wickedness. 
\v 45 And righteous men will take execute judgement on them; the judgment of an adulteress and the judgment of blood: for they are adulteresses, and blood is in their hands. 
\p
\v 46 Thus says the Lord God, Bring up a multitude upon them, and send trouble and plunder into the midst of them. 
\v 47 Stone them with the stones of a multitude, and pierce them with their swords: they will kill their sons and their daughters, and will burn up their houses. 
\v 48 I will remove ungodliness out of the land, and all the women will be instructed, and will not do according to their ungodliness. 
\v 49 Your ungodliness will be repayed upon you, and you will bear the guilt of your intentions: and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 24 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, in the ninth year, in the tenth month, on the tenth \add day\add* of the month, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, write for yourself this day, this very day, the day on which the king of Babylon laid siege to Jerusalem.
\v 3 Speak a parable to the rebellious house, and you will say to them, 
\p Thus says the Lord; Set on the caldron, and pour water into it: 
\v 4 and put the pieces into it, every prime piece, the leg and shoulder taken off from the bones, 
\v 5 taken from choice cattle, and burn the bones under them: let it boil and boil, and let its bones be boiled within it.
\p
\v 6 Therefore thus says the Lord; O bloody city, the caldron in which there is scum, and the scum has not gone out of, she has brought it forth piece by piece, no lot has fallen upon it. 
\v 7 For her blood is among her; I have set it upon a smooth rock: I have not poured it out upon the earth, so that the earth should cover it; 
\v 8 that my wrath should come up for complete vengeance to be taken: I set her blood upon a smooth rock, so as not to cover it. 
\p
\v 9 Therefore thus says the Lord, I will also make the firebrand great, 
\v 10 and I will multiply the wood, and kindle the fire, that the flesh may be consumed, and the liquid boiled away; 
\v 11 and that \add it\add* may stand upon the coals, that her brass may be thoroughly heated, and be melted among her filthiness, and her scum may be consumed, 
\v 12 and her abundant scum may not come forth from her. 
\v 13 Her scum will become shameful, because you defiled yourself: and why are you still not cleansed until I have accomplished my wrath? 
\p
\v 14 I the Lord have spoken; and it will come, and I will do \add it\add*; I will not delay, neither will I have any mercy: I will judge you, says the Lord, according to your ways, and according to your intentions: therefore I will judge you according to your bloodshed, and according to your intentions will I judge you, you unclean, notorious, and abundantly rebellious one. 
\p
\v 15 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 16 Son of man, behold I take from you the desire of your eyes by violence: you will not lament, neither will you weep. 
\v 17 You will groan for blood, and have mourning upon your loins; your hair will not be braided upon you, and your sandals \add will be\add* on your feet; you will certainly not be comforted by their lips, and you will not eat the bread of men. 
\p
\v 18 I spoke to the people in the morning, as he commanded me: and my wife died in the evening; and I did in the morning as I was commanded. 
\v 19 The people said to me, Will you not tell us what these things are that you do? 
\v 20 Then I said to them, The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 21 Say to the house of Israel, 
\p Thus says the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* profane my sanctuary, the boast of your strength, the desire of your eyes, and for which your souls are concerned; and your sons and your daughters, whom you have left, will fall by the sword. 
\v 22 You will do as I have done: you will not be comforted at their mouth, and you will not eat the bread of men. 
\v 23 Your hair \add will be\add* upon your head, and your shoes on your feet: neither will you at all lament or weep; but you will pine away in your iniquities, and will comfort every one his brother. 
\v 24 Ezekiel will be for a sign to you: according to all that I have done so will you do, when these things come; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 25 You, son of man, \add will it\add* not \add be\add* in the day when I take their strength from them, the pride of their boasting, the desires of their eyes, and the pride of their soul, their sons and their daughters, 
\v 26 that in that day he who escapes will come to you, to tell \add it\add* you in your ears? 
\v 27 In that day your mouth will be opened to him who escapes; you will speak, and will be no longer dumb: and you will be for a sign to them, and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 25 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, set your face steadfastly against the children of Ammon, and prophesy against them; 
\v 3 and you will say to the children of Ammon, 
\p Hear the word of the Lord; thus says the Lord: Although you have rejoiced against my sanctuary, because it was profaned; and against the land of Israel, because it was laid waste; and against the house of Judah, because they went into captivity; 
\v 4 therefore, behold, I \add will\add* deliver you to the children of Kedem for an inheritance, and they will lodge in you with their stuff, and they will pitch their tents in you: they will eat your fruits, and they will drink your milk. 
\v 5 I will give up the city of Ammon for camels' pastures, and the children of Ammon for a pasture of sheep: and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 6 For thus says the Lord; Because you have clapped your hands, and stamped your foot, and heartily rejoiced against the land of Israel; 
\v 7 therefore I will stretch out my hand against you, and I will make you a spoil to the nations; and I will completely destroy you from among the peoples, and I will completely cut you off from out of the lands: and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 8 Thus says the Lord; Because Moab has said, Behold, aren't the house of Israel and Judah like all the \add other\add* nations? 
\v 9 Therefore, behold, I will weaken the shoulder of Moab from his frontier cities, \add even\add* the choice land, the house of Bethasimuth above the fountain of the city, by the sea-side. 
\v 10 I have given him the children of Kedem in addition to the children of Ammon for an inheritance, that there may be no remembrance of the children of Ammon. 
\v 11 I will execute vengeance on Moab; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 12 Thus says the Lord; Because of what the Idumeans have done in taking vengeance on the house of Judah, and \add because they\add* have remembered injuries, and have exacted full recompence; 
\v 13 therefore thus says the Lord; I will also stretch out my hand upon Idumea, and will completely destroy out of it man and beast; and will make it desolate; and those who are pursued out of Thæman will fall by the sword. 
\v 14 I will execute my vengeance on Idumea by the hand of my people Israel: and they will deal in Idumea according to my anger and according to my wrath, and they will know my vengeance, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 Therefore thus says the Lord, Because the Philistines have worked revengefully, and raised up vengeance rejoicing from their heart to destroy \add the Israelites\add* to a man; 
\v 16 therefore thus says the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* stretch out my hand upon the Philistines, and will completely destroy the Cretans, and will cut off the remnant that dwell by the sea-coast. 
\v 17 I will execute great vengeance upon them; and they will know that I am the Lord, when I have brought my vengeance upon them. 
\c 26 
\p
\v 1 It happened in the eleventh year, on the first \add day\add* of the month, \add that\add* the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 2 Son of man, because \f + \fr 26:2 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor has said against Jerusalem, Aha, she is crushed: the nations are destroyed: she is turned to me: the one who was full is made desolate: 
\v 3 therefore thus says the Lord; Behold, I am against you, O \f + \fr 26:3 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor, and I will bring up many nations against you, as the sea comes up with its waves. 
\v 4 They will cast down the walls of \f + \fr 26:4 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor, and will cast down your towers: and I will scrape her dust from off her, and make her a bare rock. 
\v 5 She will be among the sea a place for repairing nets: for I have spoken \add it\add*, says the Lord: and it will be a spoil for the nations. 
\v 6 Her daughters \add which are\add* in the field will be killed with the sword, and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 7 For thus says the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* bring up against you, O \f + \fr 26:7 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon from the north: he is a king of kings, with horses, and chariots, and horsemen, and a concourse of very many nations. 
\v 8 He will kill your daughters that are in the field with the sword, and will set a watch against you, and build forts around you, and carry a rampart round against you, and set up warlike works, and array his spears against you. 
\v 9 He will cast down with his swords your walls and your towers. 
\v 10 Because of the multitude of his horses their dust will cover you, and because of the sound of his horsemen and the wheels of his chariots your walls will are shaken, when he enters into your gates, as one entering into a city from the plain. 
\v 11 With the hoofs of his horses they will trample all your streets: he will kill your people with the sword, and will bring down to the ground the support of your strength. 
\p
\v 12 He will prey upon your power, and plunder your substance, and will cast down your walls, and break down your pleasant houses: and he will cast your stones and your timber and your dust into the midst of your sea. 
\v 13 He will destroy the multitude of your musicians, and the sound of your psalteries will be heard no more. 
\v 14 I will make you a bare rock: you will be a place to spread nets upon; you will be built no more: for I the Lord have spoken \add it\add*, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 For thus says the Lord God to \f + \fr 26:15 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor; Will not the isles shake at the sound of your fall, while the wounded are groaning, while they have drawn a sword among you? 
\v 16 All the princes of the nations of the sea will come down from their thrones, and will take off their crowns from their heads, and will take off their embroidered clothing: they will be completely amazed; they will sit upon the ground, and fear their \add own\add* destruction, and will groan over you. 
\v 17 They will take up a lamentation for you, and will say to you, How are you destroyed from out of the sea, the renowned city, that brought her terror upon all her inhabitants. 
\v 18 The isles will be alarmed at the day of your fall. 
\p
\v 19 For thus says the Lord God; When I will make the city desolate, as the cities that will not be inhabited, when I have brought the deep up upon you, 
\v 20 and great waters will cover you; and I will bring you down to those who go down to the pit, to the people of old time, and will cause you to dwell in the depths of the earth, as in everlasting desolation, with those who go down to the pit, that you may not be inhabited, nor stand upon the land of life; 
\v 21 I will make you a ruin, and you will never exist again, says the Lord God. 
\c 27 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 2 You, son of man, take up a lamentation against \f + \fr 27:1 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor; 
\v 3 and you will say to \f + \fr 27:2 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor that dwells at the entrance of the sea, the trading centre of the nations from many islands, Thus says the Lord to Sor; 
\p You have said, I have clothed myself with my beauty. 
\v 4 In the heart of the sea your sons have put beauty upon you for \f + \fr 27:4 \ft Compare Heb. Beelim is probably a transliteration or corruption of a Hebrew word meaning 'borders'.\f*Beelim. 
\v 5 Cedar in Senir was employed for you in building: boards of cypress timber were taken out of Lebanon, and wood to make you masts of fir. 
\v 6 They made your oars \add of wood\add* out of the land of Basan; your sacred utensils they made of ivory, your shady houses of wood from the isles of Chetiim. 
\v 7 Fine linen with embroidery from Egypt supplied your couch, to put honour upon you, and to clothe you with blue and purple from the isles of Elisai; and they became your coverings. 
\p
\v 8 Your princes were the dwellers in Sidon, and the Aradians were your rowers: your wise men, O \f + \fr 27:8 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor, who were in you, these were your pilots. 
\v 9 The elders of the Biblians, and their wise men, who were in you, these helped your counsel: and all the ships of the sea and their rowers traded for you to the utmost west. 
\p
\v 10 Persians and Lydians and Libyans were in your army: your warriors hung in you shields and helmets; these gave \add you\add* your glory. 
\v 11 The sons of the Aradians and your army were upon your walls; there were guards in your towers: they hung their quivers on your battlements all around; these completed your beauty. 
\p
\v 12 The Carthaginians were your merchants because of the abundance of all your strength; they furnished your market with silver, and gold, and iron, and tin, and lead. 
\v 13 Greece, both the whole \add world\add*, and the adjacent coasts, these traded with you in the persons of men, and they gave \add as\add* your merchandise vessels of brass. 
\p
\v 14 Out of the house of Thogarma horses and horsemen furnished your market. 
\v 15 The sons of the Rhodians were your merchants; from the islands they multiplied your merchandise, \add even\add* elephants' teeth: and to those who came in you returned your prices, 
\v 16 \add even\add* men \add as\add* your merchandise, from the multitude of your trading \add population\add*, myrrh and embroidered works from Tharsis: Ramoth also and Chorchor furnished your market. 
\v 17 Judah and the children of Israel, these were your merchants; in the sale of grain and ointments and cassia: and they gave the best honey, and oil, and resin, to your trading \add population\add*. 
\v 18 \add The people of\add* Damascus were your merchants because of the abundance of all your power; wine out of Chelbon, and wool from Miletus; and they brought wine into your market. 
\p
\v 19 Out of Asel \add came\add* worked iron, and there is the sound of wheels among your trading \add population\add*. 
\v 20 \add The people of\add* Dædan were your merchants, with choice cattle for chariots. 
\v 21 Arabia and all the princes of Kedar, these were your traders with you, \add bringing\add* camels, and lambs, and rams, in which they trade with you. 
\v 22 The merchants of Sabba and Ramma, these were your merchants, with choice spices, and precious stones: and they brought gold to your market. 
\v 23 Charra, and Chanaa, these were your merchants: Assur, and Charman, were your merchants: 
\v 24 bringing \add for\add* merchandise blue, and choice stores bound with cords, and cypress wood. 
\v 25 Ships were your merchants, in abundance, with your trading \add population\add*: and you were filled and very heavily loaded in the heart of the sea. 
\p
\v 26 Your rowers have brought you into great waters: the south wind has broken you in the heart of the sea. 
\v 27 Your forces, and your gain, and that of your traders, and your rowers, and your pilots, and your counsellors, and those who traffic with you, and all your warriors that are in you: and all your company among you will perish in the heart of the sea, in the day of your fall. 
\p
\v 28 At the cry of your voice your pilots will be greatly terrified. 
\v 29 All the rowers and the mariners will come down from the ships, and the pilots of the sea will stand on the land. 
\v 30 They will wail over you with their voice, and cry bitterly, and put earth on their heads, and spread ashes under them. 
\p
\v 32 Their sons will take up a \add lament\add* for you, even a lamentation for \f + \fr 27:32 \ft Sor is a transliteration of the Hebrew name צֹר (Ṣōr), usually rendered Tyre in English.\f*Sor, \add saying\add*, 
\v 33 How large a reward have you gained from the sea? You have filled nations out of your abundance; and out of your mixed merchandise you have enriched all the kings of the earth. 
\v 34 Now are you broken in the sea, your traders are in the deep water, and all your company among you: all your rowers have fallen. 
\v 35 All the dwellers in the islands have mourned over you, and their kings have been completely amazed, and their face has wept. 
\v 36 Merchants from the nations have hissed at you; you are completely destroyed, and will never exist again.
\c 28 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 2 You, son of man, say to the prince of Tyre, Thus says the Lord; Because your heart has been exalted, and you have said, I am God, I have inhabited the dwelling of God in the heart of the sea; yet you are man and not God, though you have set your heart as the heart of God: 
\v 3 are you wiser than \ft Daniel here likely refers to an ancient figure (Danel) known for righteousness, not the biblical Daniel.\f*Daniel? Or have the wise not instructed you with their knowledge? 
\v 4 Have you gained power for yourself by your \add own\add* knowledge or your \add own\add* prudence, and \add gotten\add* gold and silver in your treasures? 
\v 5 By your great skill and your commerce you have multiplied your power; your heart has been lifted up by your power. 
\p
\v 6 Therefore thus says the Lord; Since you have set your heart as the heart of God; 
\v 7 because of this, behold, I \add will\add* bring on you foreign plagues from the nations; and they will draw their swords against you, and against the beauty of your knowledge, 
\v 8 and they will bring down your beauty to destruction. And they will bring you down; and you will die the death of the killed in the heart of the sea. 
\v 9 Will you indeed say, I am God, before those who kill you? Because you are man, and not God. 
\v 10 You will perish by the hands of strangers among the multitude of the uncircumcised: for I have spoken it, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 11 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 12 Son of man, take up a lamentation for the prince of Tyre, and say to him, Thus says the Lord God; You are a seal of resemblance, and crown of beauty. 
\v 13 You were in the delight of the paradise of God; you have bound upon you every precious stone, the sardius, and topaz, and emerald, and carbuncle, and sapphire, and jasper, and silver, and gold, and ligure, and agate, and amethyst, and chrysolite, and beryl, and onyx: and you have filled your treasures and your stores in you with gold. 
\v 14 From the day that you were created you \add were\add* with the cherub: I set you on the holy mount of God; you were among the stones of fire. 
\v 15 You were faultless in your days, from the day that you were created, until wickedness was found in you. 
\p
\v 16 Of the abundance of your merchandise you have filled your storehouses with wickedness, and have sinned: therefore you have been cast down wounded from the mount of God, and the cherub has brought you out of the midst of the stones of fire. 
\v 17 Your heart has been lifted up because of your beauty; your knowledge has been corrupted with your beauty: because of the multitude of your sins I have cast you to the ground, I have caused you to be put to open shame before kings. 
\v 18 Because of the multitude of your sins and the iniquities of your merchandise, I have profaned your sacred things; and I will bring fire out of the midst of you, this will devour you; and I will make you \add to be\add* ashes upon your land before all that see you. 
\v 19 All who know you among the nations will groan over you: you have gone to destruction, and you will not exist any more. 
\p
\v 20 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 21 Son of man, set your face against Sidon, and prophesy against it, 
\v 22 and say, 
\p Thus says the Lord; Behold, I am against you, O Sidon; and I will be glorified in you; and you will know that I am the Lord, when I have worked judgments in you, and I will be sanctified in you. 
\v 23 Blood and death \add will be\add* in your streets; and \add men\add* wounded with swords will fall in you and on every side of you; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\v 24 In the house of Israel there will no longer be a thorn of bitterness and a pricking briar coming from those who are all around them, who dishonoured them; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 25 Thus says the Lord God; I will also gather Israel from the nations, among whom they have been scattered, and I will be sanctified among them, and before the peoples and nations: and they will dwell upon their land, which I gave to my servant Jacob. 
\v 26 Yes, they will dwell upon it safely, and they will build houses, and plant vineyards, and dwell securely, when I will execute judgment on all that have dishonoured them, \add even\add* on those \add that are\add* all around them; and they will know that I am the Lord their God, and the God of their fathers. 
\c 29 
\p
\v 1 In the twelfth year, in the tenth month, on the first \add day\add* of the month, the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, set your face against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and prophesy against him, and against the whole of Egypt: 
\v 3 and say, 
\p Thus says the Lord; Behold, I am against Pharaoh, the great dragon that lies among his rivers, that says, The rivers are mine, and I made them. 
\v 4 I will put hooks in your jaws, and I will cause the fish of your river to stick to your sides, and I will bring you up out of the midst of your river: 
\v 5 and I will quickly cast down you and all the fish of your river: you will fall on the face of the plain, and will surely not be gathered, and will not be brought together: I have given you for food to the wild beasts of the earth and to the fowls of the sky. 
\v 6 All the dwellers in Egypt will know that I am the Lord, because you have been a staff of reed to the house of Israel. 
\v 7 When they took hold of you with their hand, you broke: and when every hand was clapped against them, and when they leaned on you, you were completely broken, and crushed the loins of them all. 
\p
\v 8 Therefore thus says the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* bring a sword upon you, and will cut off from you man and beast; 
\v 9 and the land of Egypt will be ruined and desert; and they will know that I am the Lord; because you say, The rivers are mine, and I made them. 
\p
\v 10 Therefore, behold, I am against you, and against all your rivers, and I will give up the land of Egypt to desolation, and the sword, and destruction, from Magdol and Syene even to the borders of the Ethiopians. 
\v 11 No foot of man will pass through it, and no foot of beast will pass through it, and it will not be inhabited for forty years. 
\p
\v 12 I will cause her land to be completely destroyed among a land that is desolate, and her cities will be \add desolate\add* forty years among cities that are desolate: and I will disperse Egypt among the nations, and will completely scatter them into the lands. 
\p
\v 13 Thus says the Lord; After forty years I will gather the Egyptians from the nations among whom they have been scattered; 
\v 14 and I will turn the captivity of the Egyptians, and will cause them to dwell in the land of Phathore, in the land where they were taken; 
\v 15 and it will be a base kingdom beyond all \add other\add* kingdoms; it will not be exalted over the nations any more; and I will make them few in number, so they may not be \add great\add* among the nations. 
\v 16 They will no more be to the house of Israel a confidence bringing wickedness to remembrance, when they follow after them; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 17 It happened in the twenty-seventh year, on the first \add day\add* of the first month, the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 18 Son of man, Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon caused his army to serve a great service against Tyre; every head was bald, and every shoulder peeled; yet there was no reward to him or to his army \add serving\add* against Tyre, nor for the service with which they served against it. 
\p
\v 19 Thus says the Lord God; Behold, I \add will\add* give to Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon the land of Egypt, and he will take the plunder of it, and seize the spoils of it; and \add it\add* will be a reward for his army. 
\v 20 In return for his service with which he served against Tyre, I have given him the land of Egypt; thus says the Lord God: 
\p
\v 21 In that day will a horn spring forth for all the house of Israel, and I will give you an open mouth among them; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 30 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, prophesy, and say, Thus says the Lord; Woe, woe for the day! 
\v 3 For the day of the Lord is near, a day of cloud; it will be the end of the nations. 
\p
\v 4 A sword will come upon the Egyptians, and there will be tumult in Ethiopia, and in Egypt \add men\add* will fall down killed together, and her foundations will fall. 
\v 5 Persians, and Cretans, and Lydians, and Libyans, and all the mixed multitude, and they of the children of my covenant, will fall by the sword therein. 
\v 6 The supports of Egypt will fall; and the pride of her strength will come down from Magdol to Syene: they will fall by the sword in it, says the Lord. 
\v 7 It will be made desolate among desolate lands, and their cities will be \add desolate\add* among the desolate cities: 
\v 8 and they will know that I am the Lord, when I will send fire upon Egypt, and \add when\add* all that help her will be broken. 
\v 9 In that day messengers will go forth hurrying to destroy Ethiopia completely, and there will be tumult among them in the day of Egypt: for, behold, it comes. 
\p
\v 10 Thus says the Lord God; I will also destroy the multitude of the Egyptians by the hand of Nebuchadnezzar king of Babylon, 
\v 11 his \add hand\add* and his people's; \add they are\add* plagues sent from the nations to destroy the land: and they all will unsheath their swords against Egypt, and the land will be filled with killed. 
\v 12 I will make their rivers desolate, and will destroy the land and the fulness of it by the hands of strangers: I the Lord have spoken. 
\p
\v 13 For thus says the Lord God; I will also destroy the nobles from Memphis, and the princes of Memphis out of the land of Egypt; and they will be no more. 
\v 14 I will destroy the land of Phathore, and will send fire upon Tanis, and will execute vengeance on Diospolis. 
\v 15 I will pour out my wrath upon Sais the strength of Egypt, and will destroy the multitude of Memphis. 
\v 16 I will send fire upon Egypt; and Syene will be sorely troubled; and there will be a breaking in Diospolis, and waters will be poured out. 
\v 17 The youths of Heliopolis and Bubastum will fall by the sword, and the women will go into captivity. 
\v 18 The day will be darkened in Taphnæ, when I have broken there the sceptres of Egypt: and the pride of her strength will perish there: and a cloud will cover her, and her daughters will be taken prisoners. 
\v 19 I will execute judgment on Egypt; and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 20 It happened in the eleventh year, in the first month, on the seventh \add day\add* of the month, the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 21 Son of man, I have broken the arms of Pharaoh, king of Egypt; and, behold, it has not been bound up to be healed, to have a plaster put upon it, \add or\add* to be strengthened to lay hold of the sword. 
\v 22 Therefore thus says the Lord God; Behold, I am against Pharaoh king of Egypt, and I will break his strong and outstretched arms, and will strike down his sword out of his hand. 
\v 23 I will disperse the Egyptians among the nations, and will completely scatter them among the lands. 
\p
\v 24 I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and put my sword into his hand: and he will bring it upon Egypt, and will take her plunder and seize her spoils. 
\v 25 Yes, I will strengthen the arms of the king of Babylon, and the arms of Pharaoh will fail: and they will know that I am the Lord, when I have put my sword into the hands of the king of Babylon, and he will stretch it out over the land of Egypt. 
\v 26 I will disperse the Egyptians among the nations, and completely scatter them among the lands; and they all will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 31 
\p
\v 1 It happened in the eleventh year, in the third month, on the first \add day\add* of the month, the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, say to Pharaoh king of Egypt, and to his multitude; 
\p To whom have you compared yourself in your haughtiness? 
\v 3 Behold, the Assyrian was a cypress in Lebanon, and was fair in shoots, and high in stature: his top reached to the midst of the clouds. 
\v 4 The water nourished him, the depth made him grow tall; she led her rivers all around his plants, and she sent her streams to all the trees of the field. 
\v 5 Therefore his stature was exalted above all the trees of the field, and his branches spread far by the help of much water. 
\v 6 All the birds of the sky made their nests in his boughs, and under his branches all the wild beasts of the field bred; the whole multitude of nations dwelt under his shadow. 
\v 7 He was fair in his height because of the multitude of his branches: for his roots were amidst much water. 
\v 8 Such cypresses \add as this\add* were in the garden of God; and there were no pines like his shoots, and there were no firs like his branches: no tree in the garden of God was like him in his beauty, 
\v 9 because of the multitude of his branches: and the trees of God's garden of delight envied him. 
\p
\v 10 Therefore thus says the Lord; Because you have grown great, and have set your top among the clouds, and I saw when he was exalted; 
\v 11 therefore I delivered him into the hands of the prince of the nations, and he worked his destruction. 
\v 12 Ravaging strangers from the nations have destroyed him, and have cast him down upon the mountains: his branches fell in all the valleys, and his boughs were broken in every field of the land; and all the people of the nations have gone down from their shelter, and have laid him low. 
\p
\v 13 All the birds of the sky have settled on his fallen trunk, and all the wild beasts of the field came upon his boughs: 
\v 14 in order that none of the trees by the water should exalt themselves because of their size: because they set their top among the clouds, yet they didn't continue in their high state in their place, all that drank water, all were consigned to death, to the depth of the earth, among the children of men, with those who go down to the pit. 
\p
\v 15 Thus says the Lord God; In the day when he went down to Hades, the deep mourned for him: and I stayed her floods, and restrained her abundance of water: and Lebanon saddened for him, all the trees of the field fainted for him. 
\v 16 At the sound of his fall the nations quaked, when I brought him down to Hades with those who go down to the pit: and all the trees of delight comforted him in the heart, and the choice \add plants\add* of Lebanon, all that drink water. 
\v 17 For they went down to hades with him among the killed with the sword; and his seed, \add even\add* those who dwelt under his shadow, perished in the middle of their life. 
\p
\v 18 To whom are you compared? Descend, and be debased with the trees of delight to the depth of the earth: you will lie among the uncircumcised with those who are killed by the sword. Thus will Pharaoh be, and the multitude of his host, says the Lord God. 
\c 32 
\p
\v 1 It happened in the twelfth year, in the tenth month, on the first \add day\add* of the month, \add that\add* the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, take up a lamentation for Pharaoh king of Egypt, and say to him, 
\p You have become like a lion of the nations, and like the snake that is in the sea: and you made assaults with your rivers, and disturbed the water with your feet, and trampled your rivers. 
\p
\v 3 Thus says the Lord; I will also cast over you the nets of many nations, and will bring you up with my hook: 
\v 4 and I will stretch you upon the earth: the fields will be covered \add with you\add*, and I will cause all the birds of the sky to settle upon you, and I will fill all the wild beasts of the earth \add with you\add*. 
\v 5 I will cast your flesh upon the mountains, and will saturate \add them\add* with your blood. 
\v 6 The land will be drenched with your dung, because of your multitude upon the mountains: I will fill the valleys with you. 
\v 7 I will veil the heavens when you are extinguished, and will darken its stars; I will cover the sun with a cloud, and the moon will not give her light. 
\v 8 All the \add bodies\add* that give light in the sky, will be darkened over you, and I will bring darkness upon the earth, says the Lord God. 
\p
\v 9 I will provoke to anger the heart of many people, when I will lead you captive among the nations, to a land which you have not known. 
\v 10 Many nations will mourn over you, and their kings will be completely amazed, when my sword flies in their faces, as they wait for their \add own\add* fall from the day of your fall. 
\p
\v 11 For thus says the Lord God; The sword of the king of Babylon will come upon you, 
\v 12 with the swords of mighty men; and I will cast down your strength: \add they are\add* all destroying ones from the nations, and they will destroy the pride of Egypt, and all her strength will be crushed. 
\v 13 I will destroy all her cattle from \add beside\add* the great water; and the foot of man will not trouble it any more, and the step of cattle will no more trample it. 
\v 14 Thus will their waters then be at rest, and their rivers will flow like oil, says the Lord, 
\v 15 when I will give up Egypt to destruction, and the land will be made desolate with its fullness; when I will scatter all that dwell in it, and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\v 16 There is a lamentation, and you will utter it; and the daughters of the nations will utter it, \add even\add* for Egypt, and they will mourn for it over all the strength of it, says the Lord God. 
\p
\v 17 It happened in the twelfth year, in the first month, on the fifteenth \add day\add* of the month, the word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\p
\v 18 Son of man, lament over the strength of Egypt, for the nations will bring down her daughters dead to the depth of the earth, to those who go down to the pit. 
\v 20 They will fall with him among them \add that are\add* killed with the sword, and all his strength will perish: the giants also will say to you, 
\v 21 Take your place in the depth of the pit: to whom are you superior? Yes, go down, and lie with the uncircumcised, among those killed with the sword. 
\p
\v 22 There are Assur and all his company: all \add his\add* killed have been laid there: 
\v 23 and their burial is in the depth of the pit, and his company are set all around his tomb: all the killed that fell by the sword, who had caused the fear of them \add to be\add* upon the land of the living. 
\p
\v 24 There is Ælam and all his host all around his tomb: all the killed who fell by the sword, and the uncircumcised who go down to the deep of the earth, who caused their fear to be upon the land of the living: and they have received their punishment with those who go down to the pit, 
\v 25 among the killed. 
\p
\v 26 There were laid Mosoch, and Thobel, and all his strength all around his tomb: all his killed men, all the uncircumcised, killed with the sword, who caused their fear to be in the land of the living. 
\v 27 They are laid with the giants that fell of old, who went down to Hades with \add their\add* weapons of war: and they laid their swords under their heads, but their iniquities were upon their bones, because they terrified all men during their life. 
\v 28 You will lie among the uncircumcised, with those who have been killed by the sword. 
\p
\v 29 There are laid the princes of Assur, who yielded their strength to a wound of the sword: these are laid with the killed, with those who go down to the pit. 
\p
\v 30 There are the princes of the north, \add even\add* all the captains of Assur, who go down killed \add to Hades\add*: they lie uncircumcised among the killed with the sword together with their terror and their strength, and they have received their punishment with those who go down to the pit. 
\p
\v 31 King Pharaoh will see them, and will be comforted over all their force, says the Lord God. 
\v 32 For I have caused his fear to be upon the land of the living: yet he will lie among the uncircumcised with those who are killed with the sword, \add even\add* Pharaoh, and all his multitude with him, says the Lord God. 
\c 33 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, speak to the children of your people, and you will say to them, 
\p On whatever land I will bring a sword, and the people of the land take one man of them, and set him for their watchman: 
\v 3 and he will see the sword coming upon the land, and blow the trumpet, and sound an alarm to the people; 
\v 4 and he who hears the sound of the trumpet will hear \add indeed\add*, and \add yet\add* not take heed, and the sword will come upon him, and overtake him, his blood will be upon his \add own\add* head. 
\v 5 Because he heard the sound of the trumpet, and took no heed, his blood will be upon him: but the other, because he took heed, has delivered his soul. 
\p
\v 6 But if the watchman sees the sword coming, and does not sound the trumpet, and the people do not watch; and the sword comes, and takes a soul from among them, that \add soul\add* is taken because of its wickedness; but I will require its blood at the watchman's hand. 
\p
\v 7 You, son of man, I have set you \add as\add* a watchman to the house of Israel, and you will hear a word from my mouth. 
\v 8 When I say to the sinner, You will surely die; \add if\add* you don't speak to warn the wicked from his way, the wicked himself will die in his wickedness; but will I require his blood at your hand. 
\v 9 But if you forewarn the wicked of his way to turn from it, and he doesn't turn from his way, he will die in his ungodliness; but you have delivered your own soul. 
\p
\v 10 You, son of man, say to the house of Israel; Thus have you spoken, saying, Our errors, and our iniquities weigh upon us, and we pine away in them, and how then will we live? 
\v 11 Say to them, Thus says the Lord; \add As\add* I live, I don't desire the death of the ungodly, as that the ungodly should turn from his way and live. Turn back! Turn back from your way; for why will you die, O house of Israel? 
\p
\v 12 Say to the children of your people, The righteousness of the righteous will not deliver him, in the day when he errs: and the wickedness of the ungodly will not harm him, in the day when he turns from his wickedness, but the righteous \add erring\add* will not be able to deliver himself. 
\p
\v 13 When I say to the righteous, \add You will live; and\add* he trusts in his righteousness, and will commit wickedness, none of his righteousnesses will be remembered; in his unrighteousness which he has worked, in it he will die. 
\p
\v 14 When I say to the ungodly, You will surely die; and he will turn from his sin, and do judgment and justice, 
\v 15 and return the pledge, and repay that which he has robbed, \add and\add* walk in the ordinances of life, so as to do no wrong; he will surely live, and will not die. 
\v 16 None of his sins which he has committed will be remembered: because he has worked judgment and righteousness; by them he will live. 
\p
\v 17 Yet the children of your people will say, The way of the Lord isn't straight: because their way isn't straight. 
\v 18 When the righteous turns away from his righteousness, and commits iniquities, then he will die in them. 
\v 19 When the sinner turns from his wickedness, and does justice and righteousness, he will live by them. 
\v 20 This is that of which you said, The way of the Lord is \add not\add* straight. I will judge you, O house of Israel, every one for his ways. 
\p
\v 21 It happened in the tenth year of our captivity, in the twelfth month, on the fifth \add day\add* of the month, \add that\add* one who had escaped from Jerusalem came to me, saying, The city is taken. 
\v 22 Now the hand of the Lord had come upon me in the evening, before he came; and he opened my mouth, when he came to me in the morning: and my mouth was open, it was no longer kept closed. 
\p
\v 23 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 24 Son of man, those who inhabit the desolate \add places\add* on the land of Israel say, Abraham was one, and he possessed the land: and we are more numerous; to us the land is given for a possession. 
\p
\v 25 Therefore say to them, Thus says the Lord God, 
\v 27 \add As\add* I live, surely those who are in the desolate places will fall by swords, and those who are in the open plain will be given for food to the wild beasts of the field, and those who are in the fortified \add cities\add* and those who are in the caves I will kill with pestilence. 
\v 28 I will make the land desert, and the pride of her strength will perish; and the mountains of Israel will be made desolate because of no man passing through. 
\v 29 They will know that I am the Lord; and I will make their land desert, and it will be made desolate because of all their abominations which they have worked. 
\p
\v 30 And \add as for\add* you, son of man, the children of your people are those who speak concerning you by the walls, and in the porches of the houses, and they talk one to another, saying, Let us come together, and let us hear the \add words\add* that proceed from the Lord. 
\v 31 They approach you as a people comes together, and sit before you, and hear your words, but they will not do them: for \add there is\add* falsehood in their mouth, and their heart \add goes\add* after their pollutions. 
\v 32 You are to them as the sound of a sweet, well-tuned psaltery, and they will hear your words, but they will not do them. 
\v 33 But whenever it will come \add to pass\add*, they will say, Behold, it has come: and they will know that there was a prophet among them. 
\c 34 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, prophesy against the shepherds of Israel, prophesy, and say to the shepherds, 
\p Thus says the Lord God; O shepherds of Israel, do shepherds feed themselves? Do not the shepherds feed the sheep? 
\v 3 Behold, you feed on the milk, and clothe yourselves with the wool, and kill the fat: but you don't feed my sheep. 
\v 4 The weak one you have not strengthened, and the sick you have not cherished, and the bruised you have not bound up, and the stray you have not turned back, and the lost you have not sought; and the strong you have wearied with labour. 
\v 5 My sheep were scattered, because there were no shepherds: and they became food to all the wild beasts of the field. 
\v 6 My sheep were scattered on every mountain, and on every high hill: yes, they were scattered on the face of the earth, and there was none to seek them out, nor to bring them back. 
\p
\v 7 Therefore, you shepherds, hear the word of the Lord. 
\v 8 \add As\add* I live, says the Lord God, surely because my sheep became a prey, and my sheep became food to all the wild beasts of the field, because there were no shepherds, and the shepherds didn't seek out my sheep, and the shepherds fed themselves, but didn't feed my sheep. 
\v 9 For this cause, O shepherds, 
\v 10 thus says the Lord God, Behold, I am against the shepherds; and I will require my sheep at their hands, and will turn them back that they will not feed my sheep, and the shepherds will no longer feed them; and I will deliver my sheep out of their mouth, and they will no longer be food for them. 
\p
\v 11 For thus says the Lord God, Behold, I will seek out my sheep, and will visit them. 
\v 12 As the shepherd seeks his flock, in the day when there is darkness and cloud, among the sheep that are separated: so will I seek out my sheep, and will bring them back from every place where they were scattered in the day of cloud and darkness. 
\v 13 I will bring them out from the nations, and will gather them from the lands, and will bring them into their own land, and will feed them upon the mountains of Israel, and in the valleys, and in every inhabited place of the land. 
\v 14 I will feed them in a good pasture, on a high mountain of Israel: and their folds will be there, and they will lie down, and there will they rest in perfect prosperity, and they will feed in a fat pasture on the mountains of Israel. 
\v 15 I will feed my sheep, and I will cause them to rest; and they will know that I am the Lord: thus says the Lord God. 
\v 16 I will seek that which is lost, and I will recover the stray one, and will bind up that which was broken, and will strengthen the fainting, and will guard the strong, and will feed them with judgment. 
\p
\v 17 And \add as for\add* you, you sheep, thus says the Lord God, Behold, I will distinguish between sheep and sheep, \add between\add* rams and he-goats. 
\v 18 And \add is it\add* not enough for you who you fed on the good pasture, that you trampled with your feet the remnant of your pasture? And \add that\add* you drank the standing water, \add that\add* you disturbed the residue with your feet? 
\v 19 So my sheep fed on that which you had trampled with your feet; and they drank the water that had been disturbed by your feet. 
\p
\v 20 Therefore thus says the Lord God; Behold, I will separate between the strong sheep and the weak sheep. 
\v 21 You shoved with your sides and shoulders, and pushed with your horns, and you cruelly treated all the sick. 
\v 22 Therefore I will save my sheep, and they will not be any more for a prey; and will judge between ram and ram. 
\p
\v 23 I will raise up one shepherd over them, and he will tend them, \add even\add* my servant David, and he will be their shepherd; 
\v 24 and I the Lord will be to them a God, and David a prince among them; I the Lord have spoken it. 
\v 25 I will make with David a covenant of peace, and I will completely destroy evil beasts from off the land; and they will dwell in the wilderness, and sleep in the forests. 
\v 26 I will settle them all around my mountain; and I will give you the rain, the rain of blessing. 
\v 27 The trees that are in the field will yield their fruit, and the earth will yield her strength, and they will dwell in the confidence of peace on their land, and they will know that I am the Lord, when I have broken their yoke; and I will deliver them out of the hand of those that enslaved them. 
\v 28 They will no more be a spoil to the nations, and the wild beasts of the land will no more at all devour them; and they will dwell safely, and there will be none to make them afraid. 
\v 29 I will raise up for them a plant of peace, and they will no more perish with hunger upon the land, and they will no more bear the reproach of the nations. 
\p
\v 30 They will know that I am the Lord their God, and they are my people. O house of Israel, says the Lord God, 
\v 31 you are my sheep, even the sheep of my flock, and I am the Lord your God, says the Lord God. 
\c 35 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, set your face against mount Seir, and prophesy against it, 
\v 3 and say to it, 
\p Thus says the Lord God; Behold, I am against you, O mount Seir, and I will stretch out my hand against you, and will make you a waste, and you will be made desolate. 
\v 4 I will cause desolation in your cities, and you will be desolate, and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\v 5 Because you have been a perpetual enemy, and have laid wait craftily for the house of Israel, with the hand of enemies with a sword, in the time of injustice, at the last: 
\p
\v 6 Therefore, as I live, says the Lord God, truly you have sinned even to blood, therefore blood will pursue you. 
\v 7 I will make mount Seir a waste, and desolate, and I will destroy from off it men and cattle: 
\v 8 and I will fill your hills and your valleys with killed men, and in all your plains there will fall in you men killed with the sword. 
\v 9 I will make you a perpetual desolation, and your cities will not be inhabited any more: and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 10 Because you said, The two nations and the two lands will be mine, and I will inherit them; because the Lord is there: 
\v 11 therefore, \add as\add* I live, says the Lord, I will even deal with you according to your enmity, and I will be made known to you when I will judge you: 
\v 12 and you will know that I am the Lord. I have heard the voice of your blasphemies, because you have said, The desolate mountains of Israel are given to us for food; 
\v 13 and you have spoken swelling words against me with your mouth: I have heard \add them\add*. 
\p
\v 14 Thus says the Lord; When all the earth is rejoicing, I will make you desolate. 
\v 15 You will be desolate, O mount Seir, and all Idumea; and it will be completely consumed: and you will know that I am the Lord their God. 
\c 36 
\p
\v 1 You, son of man, prophesy to the mountains of Israel, and say to the mountains of Israel, Hear the word of the Lord: 
\p
\v 2 Thus says the Lord God; Because the enemy has said against you, Aha, the old waste places have become a possession for us: 
\v 3 therefore prophesy, and say, Thus says the Lord God; Because you have been dishonoured, and hated by those all around you, that you might be a possession to the remainder of the nations, and you became a by-word, and a reproach to the nations: 
\v 4 therefore, you mountains of Israel, hear the word of the Lord; Thus says the Lord to the mountains, and to the hills, and to the streams, and to the valleys, and to \add the places\add* that have been made desolate and destroyed, and to the cities that have been deserted, and have become a spoil and a trampling to the nations that were left all around; 
\v 5 therefore thus says the Lord; Truly in the fire of my wrath have I spoken against the rest of the nations, and against all Idumea, because they have appropriated my land to themselves for a possession with joy, disregarding the lives \add of the inhabitants\add*, to destroy \add it\add* by plunder: 
\v 6 therefore prophesy concerning the land of Israel, and say to the mountains, and to the hills, and to the valleys, and to the forests, Thus says the Lord; Behold, I have spoken in my zeal and in my wrath, because you have borne the reproaches of the nations: 
\v 7 therefore I will lift up my hand against the nations that are all around you; they will bear their reproach. 
\p
\v 8 But your grapes and your fruits, O mountains of Israel, my people will eat; for their coming is near.
\v 9 For, behold, I am for you, and I will look up you, and you will be tilled and sown: 
\v 10 and I will multiply men upon you, the whole house of Israel, all of it: and the cities will be inhabited, and the desolate land will be built upon. 
\v 11 I will multiply men and cattle upon you; and I will cause you to dwell as at the beginning, and will treat you well, as in your former \add times\add*: and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\v 12 I will increase men upon you, \add even\add* my people Israel; and they will inherit you, and you will be to them for a possession; and you will be bereaved of them no more. 
\p
\v 13 Thus says the Lord God: Because they said to you, You devour men, and have been bereaved of your nation; 
\v 14 therefore you will no longer devour men, and you will no longer bereave your nation, says the Lord God. 
\v 15 The reproach of the nations will no more be heard against you, and you will no more bear the revilings of the peoples, says the Lord God. 
\p
\v 16 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 17 Son of man, the house of Israel dwelt upon their land, and defiled it by their way, and with their idols, and with their uncleannesses; and their way was before me like the uncleanness of a removed woman. 
\v 18 So I poured out my wrath upon them: 
\v 19 and I dispersed them among the nations, and completely scattered them through the lands: I judged them according to their way and according to their sin. 
\v 20 They went in among the nations, among which they went, and they profaned my holy name, while it was said of them, These are the people of the Lord, and they came forth out of his land. 
\v 21 But I spared them for the sake of my holy name, which the house of Israel profaned among the nations, among whom they went. 
\p
\v 22 Therefore say to the house of Israel, Thus says the Lord; I do not do this, O house of Israel, for your sakes, but because of my holy name, which you have profaned among the nations, among whom you went. 
\v 23 I will sanctify my great name, which was profaned among the nations, which you profaned among them; and the nations will know that I am the Lord, when I am sanctified among you before their eyes. 
\p
\v 24 I will take you out from the nations, and will gather you out of all the lands, and will bring you into your own land: 
\v 25 and I will sprinkle clean water upon you, and you will be purged from all your uncleannesses, and from all your idols, and I will cleanse you. 
\v 26 I will give you a new heart, and will put a new spirit in you: and I will take away the heart of stone out of your flesh, and will give you a heart of flesh. 
\v 27 I will put my Spirit in you, and will cause you to walk in my ordinances, and to keep my judgments, and do \add them\add*. 
\v 28 You will dwell upon the land which I gave to your fathers; and you will be my people, and I will be your God. 
\v 29 I will save you from all your uncleannesses: and I will call for the grain, and multiply it, and will not bring famine upon you. 
\v 30 I will multiply the fruit of the trees, and the produce of the field, that you may not bear the reproach of famine among the nations. 
\p
\v 31 You will remember your evil ways, and your practices that were not good, and you will be hateful in your own sight for your transgressions and for your abominations. 
\v 32 Not for your sakes do I \add this\add*, says the Lord God, \add as\add* it is known to you: be ashamed and greatly agitated for your ways, O house of Israel. 
\p
\v 33 Thus says the Lord God; In the day when I will cleanse you from all your iniquities I will also cause the cities to be inhabited, and the waste \add places\add* will be built upon: 
\v 34 and the desolate land will be cultivated, because it was desolate in the eyes of every one that passed by. 
\v 35 They will say, That desolate land is become like a garden of delight; and the waste and desolate and ruined cities are inhabited. 
\v 36 The nations, as many as will have been left all around you, will know that I the Lord have built the ruined \add cities\add* and planted the waste \add lands\add*: I the Lord have spoken, and will do \add it\add*. 
\p
\v 37 Thus says the Lord God; Yet \add for\add* this will I be sought by the house of Israel, to establish them; I will multiply them \add even\add* men as sheep; 
\v 38 as holy sheep, as the sheep of Jerusalem in her feasts; thus will the desert cities be full of flocks of men: and they will know that I \add am\add* the Lord. 
\c 37 
\p
\v 1 The hand of the Lord came upon me, and the Lord brought me forth by the Spirit, and set me among the plain, and it was full of human bones. 
\v 2 He led me all around them every way: and, behold, \add there were\add* very many on the face of the plain, very dry. 
\p
\v 3 He said to me, Son of man, will these bones live? And I said, O Lord God, you know this. 
\v 4 He said to me, Prophesy upon these bones, and you will say to them, You dry bones, hear the word of the Lord. 
\v 5 Thus says the Lord to these bones; Behold, I \add will\add* bring upon you the breath of life: 
\v 6 and I will lay sinews upon you, and will bring up flesh upon you, and will spread skin upon you, and will put my Spirit into you, and you will live; and you will know that I am the Lord. 
\p
\v 7 So I prophesied as \add the Lord\add* commanded me: and it happened while I was prophesying, that, behold, \add there was\add* a shaking, and the bones approached each one to his joint. 
\v 8 I looked, and, behold, sinews and flesh grew upon them, and skin came upon them above: but there was no breath in them. 
\v 9 He said to me, Prophesy to the wind, prophesy, son of man, and say to the wind, Thus says the Lord; Come from the four winds, and breathe upon these dead \add men\add*, and let them live. 
\v 10 So I prophesied as he commanded me, and the breath entered into them, and they lived, and stood upon their feet, a very great congregation. 
\p
\v 11 The Lord spoke to me, saying, Son of man, these bones are the whole house of Israel: and they say, Our bones have become dry, our hope has perished, we are quite spent. 
\v 12 Therefore prophesy and say, 
\p Thus says the Lord; Behold, I \add will\add* open your tombs, and will bring you up out of your tombs, and will bring you into the land of Israel. 
\v 13 You will know that I am the Lord, when I have opened your graves, that I may bring up my people from \add their\add* graves. 
\v 14 I will put my Spirit within you, and you will live, and I will place you upon your own land: and you will know that I \add am\add* the Lord; I have spoken, and will do \add it\add*, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 16 Son of man, take for yourself a rod, and write upon it, Judah, and the children of Israel his adherents; and you will take for yourself another rod, and you will inscribe it for Joseph, the rod of Ephraim, and all the children of Israel that belong to him. 
\v 17 You will join them together for yourself, so as that they should bind themselves into one stick; and they will be in your hand. 
\p
\v 18 It will come to pass, when the children of your people will say to you, Will you not tell us what you mean by these things? 
\v 19 Then you will say to them, Thus says the Lord; Behold, I will take the tribe of Joseph, which is in the hand of Ephraim, and the tribes of Israel that belong to him, and I will add them to the tribe of Judah, and they will become one rod in the hand of Judah. 
\v 20 The rods on which you wrote will be in your hand in their presence. 
\v 21 You will say to them, 
\p Thus says the Lord God; Behold, I \add will\add* take the whole house of Israel out of the midst of the nations, among whom they have gone, and I will gather them from all that are all around them, and I will bring them into the land of Israel. 
\v 22 I will make them a nation in my land, even on the mountains of Israel; and they will have one prince: and they will be no more two nations, neither they will be divided any more at all into two kingdoms: 
\v 23 so they may no more defile themselves with their idols; and I will deliver them from all their transgressions by which they have sinned, and will cleanse them; and they will be to me a people, and I the Lord will be to them a God. 
\p
\v 24 My servant David \add will be\add* a prince among them: there will be one shepherd of \add them\add* all; for they will walk in my ordinances, and keep my judgments, and do them. 
\v 25 They will dwell in their land, which I have given to my servant Jacob, where their fathers dwelt; and they will dwell upon it: and David my servant \add will be their\add* prince forever. 
\p
\v 26 I will make with them a covenant of peace; it will be an everlasting covenant with them; and I will establish my sanctuary among them forever. 
\v 27 My tabernacle will be among them; and I will be to them a God, and they will be my people. 
\v 28 The nations will know that I am the Lord who sanctifies them, when my sanctuary is among them forever. 
\c 38 
\p
\v 1 The word of the Lord came to me, saying, 
\v 2 Son of man, set your face against Gog, and the land of Magog, Rhos, prince of Mesoch and Thobel, and prophesy against him, 
\v 3 and say to him, Thus says the Lord God; 
\p Behold, I am against you, Rhos prince of Mesoch and Thobel: 
\v 4 and I will gather you, and all your host, horses and horsemen, all wearing breast-plates, with a great multitude, shields and helmets and swords: 
\v 5 Persians, and Ethiopians, and Libyans; all with helmets and shields. 
\v 6 Gomer, and all belonging to him; the house of Thorgama, from the end of the north, and all belonging to him; and many nations with you. 
\p
\v 7 Be prepared, prepare yourself, you, and all your multitude that is assembled with you, and you will be to me for a guard. 
\v 8 He will be prepared after many days, and he will come at the end of years, and will come to a land that is brought back from the sword, when \add the people\add* are gathered from many nations against the land of Israel, which was entirely desolate: and he has come forth out of the nations, and they will all dwell securely. 
\v 9 You will go up as rain, and will arrive as a cloud to cover the land, and there will be, and all that are about you, and many nations with you. 
\p
\v 10 Thus says the Lord God; It will also come to pass in that day, that thoughts will come up into your heart, and you will devise evil plans. 
\v 11 You will say, I will go up to the rejected land; I will come upon those who are at ease in tranquillity, and dwelling in peace, all inhabiting a land in which there is no wall, nor bars, nor have they doors; 
\v 12 to seize plunder, and to take their spoil; to turn my hands against the desolate land that is \add now\add* inhabited, and against a nation that is gathered from many nations, that have acquired property, dwelling among the land. 
\v 13 Sabba, and Dædan, and Carthaginian merchants, and all their villages will say to you, You have come for plunder to take a prey, and to get spoils: you have gathered your multitude to take silver and gold, to carry off property, to take spoils. 
\p
\v 14 Therefore prophesy, son of man, and say to Gog, Thus says the Lord; Will you not arise in that day, when my people Israel are dwelling securely, 
\v 15 and come out of your place from the farthest north, and many nations with you? All of them mounted on horses, a great gathering, and a large force? 
\v 16 You will come up upon my people Israel as a cloud to cover the land; it will come to pass in the last days, that I will bring you up upon my land, that all the nations may know me, when I am sanctified in you before them. 
\p
\v 17 Thus says the Lord God, to Gog; You are \add he\add* concerning whom I spoke in former times, by the hand of my servants the prophets of Israel, in those days and years, that I would bring you up against them. 
\v 18 It will come to pass in that day, in the day when Gog will come against the land of Israel, says the Lord God, 
\v 19 \add that\add* my wrath and my zeal will arise, I have spoken in the fire of my anger, truly in that day there will be a great shaking in the land of Israel; 
\v 20 and the fish of the sea will quake at the presence of the Lord, and the birds of the sky and the wild beasts of the field, and all the reptiles that creep upon the earth, and all the men who are on the face of the earth; and the mountains will be rent, and the valleys will fall, and every wall on the land will fall. 
\v 21 I will summon against it even every fear, says the Lord: the sword of \add every\add* man will be against his brother. 
\v 22 I will judge him with pestilence, and blood, and sweeping rain, and hailstones; and I will rain upon him fire and brimstone, and upon all who are with him, and upon many nations with him. 
\p
\v 23 I will be magnified, and sanctified, and glorified; and I will be known in the presence of many nations, and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\c 39 
\p
\v 1 You, son of man, prophesy against Gog, and say, Thus says the Lord; Behold, I am against you, O Gog, Rhos prince of Mesoch and Thobel: 
\v 2 and I will assemble you, and guide you, and raise you up on the extremity of the north, and I will bring you up upon the mountains of Israel. 
\v 3 I will destroy your bow out of your left hand, and your arrows out of your right hand, and I will cast you down on the mountains of Israel; 
\v 4 and you and all that belong to you will fall, and the nations that are with you will be given to multitudes of birds, \add even\add* to every fowl, and I have given you to all the wild beasts of the field to be devoured. 
\v 5 You will fall on the face of the field: for I have spoken \add it\add*, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 6 I will send a fire upon Gog, and the islands will be securely inhabited: and they will know that I am the Lord. 
\v 7 My holy name will be known among my people Israel; and my holy name will no more be profaned: and the nations will know that I am the Lord, the Holy \add One\add* in Israel. 
\v 8 Behold it has come, and you will know that it will be, says the Lord God; this is the day concerning which I have spoken. 
\p
\v 9 Those who inhabit the cities of Israel will come forth, and make a fire with the arms, the shields and spears, and bows and arrows, and hand-staves, and lances, and they will keep fire burning with them for seven years: 
\v 10 and they will not take any wood out of the field, neither will they cut any out of the forests, but they will burn the weapons with fire: and they will plunder those that plundered them, and spoil those that spoiled them, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 11 It will come to pass \add that\add* in that day I will give to Gog a place of renown, a tomb in Israel, the burial-place of those who approach the sea: and they will build all around the outlet of the valley, and there they will bury Gog and all his multitude: and \add the place\add* will then be called the burial-place of Gog. 
\v 12 The house of Israel will bury them, that the land may be cleansed in the space of seven months. 
\v 13 Yes, all the people of the land will bury them; and it will be to them a \add place\add* of renown in the day wherein it was glorified, says the Lord. 
\v 14 They will appoint men continually to go over the land, to bury those who have been left on the face of the earth, to cleanse it after the space of seven months, and they will seek \add them\add* out. 
\v 15 Every one that goes through the land, and sees a man's bone, will set up a mark by it, until the buriers will have buried it in the valley, the burial-place of Gog. 
\v 16 For the name of the city \add will be\add* Burial-place: so the land will be cleansed. 
\p
\v 17 You, son of man, say, Thus says the Lord; Say to every winged bird, and to all the wild beasts of the field, 
\p Gather yourselves, and come; gather yourselves from all \add places\add* all around to my sacrifice, which I have made for you, \add even\add* a great sacrifice on the mountains of Israel, and you will eat flesh, and drink blood. 
\v 18 You will eat the flesh of mighty men, and you will drink the blood of the princes of the earth, rams, and calves and goats, and they are all fatted calves. 
\v 19 You will eat fat till you are full, and will drink wine till you are drunk, of my sacrifice which I have prepared for you. 
\v 20 You will be filled at my table, \add eating\add* horse, and rider, and mighty man, and every warrior, says the Lord. 
\p
\v 21 I will set my glory among you, and all the nations will see my judgment which I have worked, and my hand which I have brought upon them. 
\v 22 The house of Israel will know that I am the Lord their God, from this day and onwards. 
\p
\v 23 All the nations will know that the house of Israel were led captive because of their sins, because they rebelled against me, and I turned away my face from them, and delivered them into the hands of their enemies, and they all fell by the sword. 
\v 24 According to their uncleannesses and according to their transgressions did I deal with them, and I turned away my face from them. 
\p
\v 25 Therefore thus says the Lord God, I will now turn back captivity in Jacob, and will have mercy on the house of Israel, and will be zealous for the sake of my holy name. 
\v 26 They will bear their reproach, and the wickedness which they committed when they dwelt upon their land in peace. Yet there will be none to terrify \add them\add* 
\v 27 when I have brought them back from the nations, and gathered them out of the lands of the nations: and I will be sanctified among them in the presence of the nations. 
\v 28 They will know that I am the Lord their God, when I have been manifested to them among the nations. 
\v 29 I will no more turn away my face from them, because I have poured out my wrath upon the house of Israel, says the Lord God. 
\c 40 
\p
\v 1 It happened in the twenty-fifth year of our captivity, in the first month, on the tenth \add day\add* of the month, in the fourteenth year after the taking of the city, in that day the hand of the Lord was upon me, and brought me 
\v 2 in a vision of God into the land of Israel, and set me on a very high mountain, and upon it \add there was\add* as it were the frame of a city before \add me\add*. 
\p
\v 3 He brought me in there, and, behold, \add there was\add* a man, and the appearance of him was as the appearance of shining brass, and in his hand was a builder's line, and a measuring reed; and he stood at the gate. 
\v 4 The man said to me, 
\p Look with your eyes at him whom you have seen, son of man, and hear with your ears, and lay up in your heart all things that I show you; for you have come in here that \add I\add* might show you, and you will show all things that you see to the house of Israel. 
\p
\v 5 Behold a wall all around the house without, and in the man's hand a reed, the measure \add of it was\add* six cubits by the cubit, and a span: and he measured across the front wall; the breadth was equal to the reed, and the length of it equal to the reed. 
\p
\v 6 He entered by seven steps into the gate that looks eastward, and he measured across the porch of the gate equal to the reed. 
\v 7 The chamber was equal in length to the reed, and equal in breadth to the reed; and the porch between the chambers six cubits; and the second chamber equal in breadth to the reed, and equal in length to the reed, and the porch five cubits. 
\v 8 The third chamber equal in length to the reed, and equal in breadth to the reed. 
\v 9 The porch of the gateway (near the porch of the gate) eight cubits; and its posts two cubits; and the porch of the gate was inward: 
\v 10 and the chambers of the gate of the chamber in front \add were\add* three on one side and three on the other, and \add there was\add* one measure to the three: \add there was\add* one measure to the porches on this side and on that. 
\v 11 He measured the breadth of the door of the gateway, ten cubits; and the breadth of the gateway thirteen cubits. 
\v 12 The space before the chambers was narrowed to a cubit in front of the chambers on this side and on that side: and the chamber was six cubits this way, and six cubits that way. 
\p
\v 13 He measured the gate from the wall of one chamber to the wall of the other chamber: the breadth was twenty-five cubits, the one gate over against the other gate. 
\v 14 The open space of the porch of the gate without, was twenty cubits to the chambers all around the gate. 
\v 15 The open space of the gate without to the open space of the porch of the gate within was fifty cubits. 
\p
\v 16 And \add there were\add* secret windows to the chambers, and to the porches within the gate of the court all around, and in the same manner windows to the porches all around within: and on the porch \add there were\add* palm-trees on this side and on that side. 
\p
\v 17 He brought me into the inner court, and, behold, \add there were\add* chambers, and colonnades all around the court; thirty chambers within the ranges of columns. 
\v 18 The porticos were behind the gates; according to the length of the gates, was the lower colonnade. 
\v 19 He measured the breadth of the court, from the open space of the outer gate inwards to the open space of the gate looking outwards: a hundred cubits \add was the distance to the place\add* of the gate looking eastward: and he brought me to the north; 
\v 20 and behold a gate looking northwards \add belonging to\add* the outer court, and he measured it, both the length of it and the breadth; 
\v 21 and the chambers, three on this side and three on that; and the posts, and the porches, and the palm-trees of it: and they were according to the measures of the gate that looks eastward: the length of it was fifty cubits, and the breadth of it was twenty-five cubits. 
\v 22 Its windows, and its porches, and its palm-trees, were according to \add the dimensions of\add* the gate looking eastward; and they went up to it by seven steps; and the porches were within. 
\v 23 And \add there was\add* a gate to the inner court looking toward the north gate, after the manner of the gate looking toward the east; and he measured the court from gate to gate, a hundred cubits. 
\p
\v 24 He brought me to the south side, and behold a gate looking southwards: and he measured it, and its chambers, and its posts, and its porches, according to these dimensions. 
\v 25 Its windows and its porches all around were according to the windows of the porch: the length of it was fifty cubits, and the breadth of it was twenty-five cubits. 
\v 26 It had seven steps, and porches within: and it \add had\add* palm-trees on the posts, one on one side, and one on the other side. 
\v 27 And \add there was\add* a gate opposite the gate of the inner court southward: and he measured the court from gate to gate, a hundred cubits in breadth southward. 
\p
\v 28 He brought me into the inner court of the south gate: and he measured the gate according to these measures; 
\v 29 and the chambers, and the posts, and the porches, according to these measures: and \add there were\add* windows to it and to the porches all around: its length was fifty cubits, and \add its\add* breadth twenty-five cubits, 
\v 31 from the porch to the outer court: and \add there were\add* palm-trees to the post \add of it\add*, and eight steps. 
\p
\v 32 He brought me in at the gate that looks eastward: and he measured it according to these measures: 
\v 33 and the chambers, and the posts, and the porches according to these measures: and \add there were\add* windows to it, and porches all around: the length of it was fifty cubits, and the breadth of it twenty-five cubits. 
\v 34 And \add there were\add* porches \add opening\add* into the inner court, and palm-trees on the posts on this side and on that side: and it \add had\add* eight steps. 
\p
\v 35 He brought me in at the northern gate, and measured \add it\add* according to these measures; 
\v 36 and the chambers, and the posts, and the porches: and it \add had\add* windows all around, and \add it had\add* its porches: the length of it was fifty cubits, and the breadth twenty-five cubits. 
\v 37 Its porches were toward the inner court; and \add there were\add* palm-trees to the posts on this side and on that side: and it \add had\add* eight steps. 
\p
\v 38 Its chambers and its door-ways, and its porches at the second gate \add served as\add* a drain, 
\v 39 that they might kill in it the sin-offerings, and the trespass-offerings. 
\v 40 Behind the drain for the whole-burnt-offerings at the north \add gate\add*, two tables eastward behind the second gate; and \add behind\add* the porch of the gate two tables eastward. 
\v 41 Four on one side and four on the other side behind the gate; upon them they kill the victims, in front of the eight tables of sacrifices. 
\v 42 And \add there were\add* four tables of hewn stone for whole-burnt-offerings, the breadth \add of them was\add* a cubit and a half, and the length \add of them\add* two cubits \add and\add* a half, and \add their\add* height was a cubit: on them they will place the instruments with which they kill there the whole-burnt-offerings and the victims. 
\v 43 They will have within a border of hewn stone all around of a span broad, and over the tables above screens for covering \add them\add* from the wet and from the heat. 
\p
\v 44 He brought me into the inner court, and behold \add there were\add* two chambers in the inner court, one behind the gate looking to the north, turning southward, and one behind the southern gate, but which looks to the north. 
\v 45 He said to me, This chamber that looks to the south, is for the priests that keep the charge of the house. 
\v 46 The chamber that looks to the north is for the priests that keep the charge of the altar: they are the sons of Sadduc, those of the tribe of Levi who draw near to the Lord to serve him. 
\p
\v 47 He measured the court, the length \add whereof was\add* a hundred cubits, and the breadth a hundred cubits, on its four sides; and the altar in front of the house. 
\v 48 He brought me into the porch of the house; and he measured the post of the porch, the breadth was five cubits on one side and five cubits on the other side; and the breadth of the door \add was\add* fourteen cubits, and the side-pieces of the door of the porch \add were\add* three cubits on one side, and three cubits on the other side. 
\v 49 The length of the porch was twenty cubits, and the breadth twelve cubits; and they went up to it by ten steps; and \add there were\add* pillars to the porch, one on this side and one on that side. 
\c 41 
\p
\v 1 He brought me into the temple, the porch of which he measured, six cubits the breadth on one side, and six cubits the breadth of the porch on the other side. 
\v 2 The breadth of the gateway was ten cubits, and the side-pieces of the gateway were five cubits on this side, and five cubits on that side: and he measured the length of it, forty cubits, and the breadth, twenty cubits. 
\p
\v 3 He went into the inner court, and measured the post of the door, two cubits; and the door, six cubits; and the side-pieces of the door, seven cubits on one side, and seven cubits on the other side. 
\v 4 He measured the length of the doors, forty cubits; and the breadth, twenty cubits, in front of the temple: and he said, This is the holy of holies. 
\p
\v 5 He measured the wall of the house, six cubits: and the breadth of \add each\add* side, four cubits all around. 
\v 6 The sides were twice ninety, side against side; and \add there was\add* a space in the wall of the house at the sides all around, that they should be for those who take hold of them to see, that they should not at all touch the walls of the house. 
\v 7 The breadth of the upper side \add was made\add* according to the projection out of the wall, against the upper one all around the house, that it might be enlarged above, and that \add men\add* might go up to the upper chambers from those below, and from the ground-sills to the third story. 
\p
\v 8 As for the height of the house all around, \add each\add* space between the sides was equal to a reed of six cubits; 
\v 9 and the breadth of the wall of each side without was five cubits; and the spaces that were left between the sides of the house, 
\v 10 and between the chambers, were a width of twenty cubits, the circumference of the house. 
\p
\v 11 The doors of the chambers were toward the space left by the one door that looked northward, and \add there was\add* one door southward; and the breadth of the remaining open space \add was\add* five cubits in extent all around. 
\p
\v 12 The partition \add wall\add* in front of the remaining space, toward the west, was seventy cubits in breadth; the breadth of the partition wall was five cubits all around, and the length of it ninety cubits. 
\v 13 He measured in front of the house a length of a hundred cubits, and the remaining spaces and the partitions; and the walls of it were in length a hundred cubits. 
\v 14 The breadth in front of the house, and the remaining \add spaces\add* before \add it were\add* a hundred cubits. 
\p
\v 15 He measured the length of the partition in front of the space left by the back parts of that house; and the \add spaces\add* left on this side and on that side were in length a hundred cubits: and the temple and the corners and the outer porch were panelled. 
\v 16 The windows were latticed, \add giving\add* light all around to the three \add stories\add*, so as to look through: and the house and the parts adjoining were planked all around, and \add so was\add* the floor, and from the floor up to the windows, and the window \add shutters\add* folded back in three parts for one to look through. 
\v 17 Almost all the way to the inner, and close to the outer \add side\add*, and upon all the wall all around within and without, 
\v 18 were carved cherubs and palm-trees between the cherubs, \add and each\add* cherub \add had\add* two faces. 
\v 19 The face of a man was toward one palm-tree on this side and on that side, and the face of a lion toward another palm-tree on this side and on that side: the house was carved all round. 
\v 20 From the floor to the ceiling were cherubs and palm-trees carved. 
\p
\v 21 The holy place and the temple opened on four sides; in front of the holy places the appearance was as the look of 
\v 22 a wooden altar, the height of it three cubits, and the length two cubits, and the breadth two cubits; and it had horns, and the base of it and the sides of it were of wood: and he said to me, This is the table, which is before the face of the Lord. 
\p
\v 23 The temple \add had\add* two doors, and the sanctuary \add had\add* two doors, with two turning leaves \add apiece\add*; 
\v 24 two leaves to the one, and two leaves to the other door. 
\v 25 And \add there was\add* carved work upon them, and cherubs on the doors of the temple, and palm-trees according to the carving of the sanctuary; and \add there were\add* stout planks in front of the porch without. 
\p
\v 26 And \add there were\add* secret windows; and he measured from side to side, to the roofing of the porch; and the sides of the house were closely planked. 
\c 42 
\p
\v 1 He brought me into the inner court eastward, opposite the northern gate: and he brought me in, and behold five chambers near the vacant space, and near the northern partition, 
\v 2 a hundred cubits in length toward the north, and in breadth fifty, 
\v 3 ornamented accordingly as the gates of the inner court, and arranged accordingly as the colonnades of the outer court, \add with\add* triple porticos fronting one another. 
\v 4 In front of the chambers was a walk ten cubits in breadth, the length \add reaching\add* to a hundred cubits; and their doors were northward. 
\v 5 The upper walks were in like manner: for the colonnade projected from it, \add even\add* from the range of columns below, and \add there was\add* a space between; so \add were there\add* a colonnade and a space between, and so \add were there\add* two porticos. 
\v 6 For they were triple, and they didn't have pillars like the pillars of the outer ones: therefore they projected from the lower ones and the middle ones from the ground. 
\p
\v 7 And \add there was\add* light without, corresponding to the chambers of the outer court looking toward the front of the northern chambers; the length \add of them was\add* fifty cubits. 
\v 8 For the length of the chambers looking toward the inner court was fifty cubits, and these are the ones that front the others; the whole was a hundred cubits. 
\p
\v 9 And \add there were\add* doors of these chambers for an outlet towards the east, so that one should go through them out of the outer court, 
\v 10 by the opening of the walk at the corner; and the south parts were toward the south, toward the remaining space, and toward the partition, and \add so were\add* the chambers. 
\v 11 The walk was in front of them, according to the measures of the chambers toward the north, both according to the length of them, and according to the breadth of them, and according to all their openings, and according to all their turnings, and according to their lights, and according to their doors. 
\v 12 \add So were the measures\add* of the chambers toward the south, and according to the doors at the entrance of the walk, as it were the distance of a reed for light, and eastward as one went in by them. 
\p
\v 13 He said to me, The chambers toward the north, and the chambers toward the south, in front of the void spaces, these are the chambers of the sanctuary, wherein the priests the sons of Sadduc, who draw near to the Lord, will eat the most holy things: and there will they lay the most holy things, and the food-offering, and the sin-offerings, and the trespass-offerings; because the place is holy. 
\v 14 None will go in there except the priests, \add and\add* they will not go forth from the holy place into the outer court, that those who draw near \add to me\add* may be continually holy, and may not touch their garments in which they minister, \add with defilement\add*, for they are holy; and they will put on other garments whenever they come in contact with the people. 
\p
\v 15 So the measurement of the house within was accomplished: and he brought me forth by the way of the gate that looks eastward, and measured the plan of the house all around in order. 
\p
\v 16 He stood behind the gate looking eastward, and measured five hundred \add cubits\add* with the measuring reed. 
\v 17 He turned to the north and measured in front of the north \add side\add* five hundred cubits with the measuring reed. 
\v 18 He turned to the west, and measured in front of the west side, five hundred \add cubits\add* with the measuring reed. 
\v 19 He turned to the south, and measured in front of the south side, five hundred \add cubits\add* by the measuring reed. 
\v 20 The \add four sides he measured\add* by the same reed, and he marked out the house and the circumference of the parts all around, \add a space\add* of five hundred \add cubits\add* eastward, and a breadth of five hundred cubits, to make a division between the sanctuary and the outer wall, that \add belonged to\add* the design of the house. 
\c 43 
\p
\v 1 Moreover he brought me to the gate looking eastward, and led me forth. 
\v 2 And, behold, the glory of the God of Israel came by the eastern way; and \add there was\add* a voice of an army, as the sound of many redoubling \add their shouts\add*, and the earth shone like light from the glory all around. 
\v 3 The vision which I saw was like the vision which I saw when I went in to anoint the city: and the vision of the chariot which I saw was like the vision which I saw at the river Chobar; and I fell upon my face. 
\p
\v 4 The glory of the Lord came into the house, by the way of the gate looking eastward. 
\v 5 The Spirit took me up, and brought me into the inner court; and, behold, the house of the Lord was full of glory. 
\v 6 I stood, and behold \add there was\add* a voice out of the house of one speaking to me, and a man stood near me, 
\v 7 and he said to me, 
\p Son of man, you have seen the place of my throne, and the place of the soles of my feet, in which my name will dwell among the house of Israel forever; and the house of Israel will no more profane my holy name, they and their princes, by their prostitution, or by the murders of \add their\add* princes among them; 
\v 8 when they set my door-way by their door-way, and my thresholds near to their thresholds: and they made my wall as it were joining myself and them, and they profaned my holy name with their iniquities which they worked: and I destroyed them in my wrath and with slaughter. 
\v 9 Now let them put away from me their prostitution, and the murders of their princes, and I will dwell among them forever. 
\p
\v 10 You, son of man, show the house to the house of Israel, so they may cease from their sins; and \add show\add* its aspect and the arrangement of it. 
\v 11 They will bear their punishment for all the things that they have done: and you will describe the house, and its entrances, and its plan, and all its ordinances, and you will make known to them all its regulations, and describe \add them\add* before them: and they will keep all my commandments, and all my ordinances, and do them. 
\p
\v 12 You will show the plan of the house on the top of the mountain: all its limits all around \add will be\add* most holy. 
\p
\v 13 These are the measures of the altar by the cubit of a cubit and a span, the cavity \add will be\add* a cubit deep, and a cubit will be the breadth, and the border on the rim of it all around will be a span: and this \add will be\add* the height of the altar 
\v 14 from the bottom at the commencement of the hollow part to this great mercy-seat, from beneath was two cubits, and the breadth was a cubit; and from the little mercy-seat to the great mercy-seat, four cubits, and the breadth was a cubit. 
\v 15 The altar \add will be\add* four cubits; and from the altar and above the horns a cubit. 
\v 16 The altar \add will be\add* of the length of twelve cubits, by twelve cubits \add in breadth\add*, square upon its four sides. 
\p
\v 17 The mercy-seat \add will be\add* fourteen cubits in length, by fourteen cubits in breadth on its four sides; and \add there will be\add* a border to it carried all around it of half a cubit; and the rim of it \add will be\add* a cubit all around; and the steps of it looking eastward. 
\p
\v 18 He said to me, Son of man, thus says the Lord God of Israel; These are the ordinances of the altar in the day of its being made, to offer upon it whole-burnt-offerings, and to pour blood upon it. 
\v 19 You will appoint to the priests the Levites of the seed of Sadduc, that draw near to me, says the Lord God, to minister to me, a calf of the herd for a sin-offering. 
\v 20 They will take of its blood, and will put \add it\add* on the four horns of the altar, and upon the four corners of the atonement hearth, and upon the base all around, and they will make atonement for it. 
\v 21 They will take the calf of the sin-offering, and it will be consumed by fire in the separate place of the house, outside the sanctuary. 
\v 22 On the second day they will take two kids of the goats without blemish for a sin-offering; and they will make atonement for the altar, as they made atonement with the calf. 
\v 23 After they have finished the atonement, they will bring an unblemished calf of the herd, and an unblemished ram of the flock. 
\v 24 You will offer \add them\add* before the Lord, and the priests will sprinkle salt upon them, and will offer them up \add as\add* whole-burnt-offerings to the Lord. 
\p
\v 25 Seven days will you offer a kid daily for a sin-offering, and a calf of the herd, and a ram out of the flock: they will sacrifice them unblemished for seven days: 
\v 26 and they will make atonement for the altar, and will purge it; and they will consecrate themselves. 
\v 27 It will come to pass from the eighth day and onward, \add that\add* the priests will offer your whole-burnt-offerings on the altar, and your peace-offerings; and I will accept you, says the Lord. 
\c 44 
\p
\v 1 Then he brought me back by the way of the outer gate of the sanctuary that looks eastward; and it was shut. 
\v 2 The Lord said to me, This gate will be shut, it will not be opened, and no one will pass through it; for the Lord God of Israel will enter by it, and it will be shut. 
\v 3 For the prince, he will sit in it, to eat bread before the Lord; he will go in by the way of the porch of the gate, and will go forth by the way of the same. 
\p
\v 4 He brought me in by the way of the gate that looks northward, in front of the house: and I looked, and, behold, the house was full of the glory of the Lord: and I fell upon my face. 
\v 5 The Lord said to me, Son of man, pay attention with your heart, and see with \add your\add* eyes, and hear with your ears all that I say to you, according to all the ordinances of the house of the Lord, and all the regulations of it; and you will pay attention well to the entrance of the house, according to all its outlets, in all the holy things. 
\v 6 You will say to the rebellious house, \add even\add* to the house of Israel, Thus says the Lord God; Let it suffice you \add to have committed\add* all your iniquities, O house of Israel! 
\v 7 that you have brought in aliens, uncircumcised in heart, and uncircumcised in flesh, to be in my sanctuary, and to profane it, when you offered bread, flesh, and blood; and you transgressed my covenant by all your iniquities; 
\v 8 and you appointed \add others\add* to keep the charges in my sanctuary. 
\p
\v 9 Therefore thus says the Lord God; No alien, uncircumcised in heart or uncircumcised in flesh, will enter into my sanctuary, of all the children of strangers that are among the house of Israel. 
\p
\v 10 But as for the Levites who departed far from me when Israel went astray from me after their imaginations, they will even bear their wickedness. 
\v 11 Yet they will minister in my sanctuary, \add being\add* porters at the gates of the house, and serving the house: they will kill the victims and the whole-burnt-offerings for the people, and they will stand before the people to minister to them. 
\v 12 Because they ministered to them before their idols, and it became to the house of Israel a punishment of wickedness; therefore have I lifted up my hand against them, says the Lord God. 
\v 13 They will not draw near to me to minister to me in the priests' office, nor to approach the holy things of the children of Israel, nor \add to approach\add* my holy of holies: but they will bear their reproach for the error wherein they erred. 
\v 14 They will bring them to keep the charges of the house, for all the service of it, and for all that they will do. 
\p
\v 15 The priests the Levites, the sons of Sadduc, who kept the charges of my sanctuary when the house of Israel went astray from me, these will draw near to me to minister to me, and will stand before my face, to offer sacrifice to me, the fat and the blood, says the Lord God. 
\v 16 These will enter into my sanctuary, and these will approach my table, to minister to me, and they will keep my charges. 
\p
\v 17 It will come to pass when they enter the gates of the inner court, \add that\add* they will put on linen robes; and they will not put on woollen garments when they minister at the gate of the inner court. 
\v 18 They will have linen mitres upon their heads, and will have linen drawers upon their loins; and they will not tightly gird themselves. 
\v 19 When they go out into the outer court to the people, they will take off their robes, in which they minister; and they will lay them up in the chambers of the sanctuary, and will put on other robes, and they will not sanctify the people with their robes. 
\v 20 They will not shave their heads, nor will they pluck off their hair; they will carefully cover their heads. 
\v 21 No priest will drink any wine, when they go into the inner court. 
\v 22 Neither will they take to themselves as wife a widow, or one who is put away, but a virgin of the seed of Israel: but if there should happen to be a priest's widow, they will take \add her\add*. 
\p
\v 23 They will teach my people \add to distinguish\add* between holy and profane, and they will make known to them \add the difference\add* between unclean and clean. 
\v 24 These will pay attention at a judgment of blood to decide it: they will rightly observe my ordinances, and judge my judgments, and keep my statutes and my commandments in all my feasts; and they will hallow my sabbaths. 
\p
\v 25 They will not go in to the dead body of a man to defile themselves: only \add a priest\add* may defile himself for a father, or for a mother, or for a son, or for a daughter, or for a brother, or for his sister, who has not been married. 
\v 26 After he has been cleansed, let him number to himself seven days. 
\v 27 On whatever day they will enter into the inner court to minister in the holy place, they will bring an atonement, says the Lord God. 
\p
\v 28 It will be to them for an inheritance: I am their inheritance: and no possession will be given them among the children of Israel; for I am their possession. 
\v 29 These will eat the food-offerings, and the sin-offerings, and the trespass-offerings; and every special offering in Israel will be theirs. 
\v 30 \add And\add* the first-fruits of all things, and the first-born of all \add animals\add* and all offerings, of all your first-fruits there will be \add a share\add* for the priests; and you will give your earliest produce to the priest, to bring your blessings upon your houses. 
\v 31 The priests will eat no bird or beast that dies by itself, or is taken by wild beasts. 
\c 45 
\p
\v 1 When you measure the land for inheritance, you will set apart first-fruits to the Lord, a holy space of the land, in length twenty-five thousand \add reeds\add*, and in breadth twenty thousand; it will be holy in all the borders of it all around. 
\v 2 There will be a sanctuary out of this, five hundred \add reeds in length\add* by five hundred in breadth, a square all around; and \add there will be\add* a vacant space \add beyond\add* this of fifty cubits all around. 
\v 3 Out of this measurement will you measure the length twenty-five thousand, and the breadth twenty thousand: and in it will be the holy of holies. 
\v 4 Of the land will be \add a portion\add* for the priests that minister in the holy place, and it will be for those who draw near to minister to the Lord: and it will be to them a place for houses set apart for their sacred office; 
\v 5 the length \add will be\add* twenty-five thousand, and the breadth twenty thousand: and the Levites that pay attention the house, they will have cities to dwell in for a possession. 
\p
\v 6 You will appoint \add for\add* the possession of the city five thousand in breadth, and in length twenty-five thousand: after the manner of the first-fruits of the holy portion, they will be for all the house of Israel. 
\p
\v 7 The prince \add will have a portion\add* out of this, and out of this \add there will be a portion\add* for the first-fruits of the sanctuary, \add and\add* for the possession of the city, in front of the first-fruits of the sanctuary, and in front of the possession of the city westward, and from the western parts eastward: and the length \add will be\add* equal to one of the parts of the western borders, and the length \add will be\add* to the eastern borders of the land. 
\v 8 He will have it for a possession in Israel: and the princes of Israel will no more oppress my people; but the house of Israel will inherit the land according to their tribes. 
\p
\v 9 Thus says the Lord God; Let it suffice you, you princes of Israel: remove injustice and misery, execute judgment and justice; take away oppression from my people, says the Lord God. 
\v 10 You will have honest \f + \fr 45:10 \ft The three Greek words in this verse, ζυγός, μέτρον and χοῖνιξ capture measurements of weight, length/area and dry volume.\f*scales, and an honest measure, and an honest dry measure. 
\v 11 In like manner there will be one dry measure as a measure of capacity; the tenth of the gomor \add will be\add* the dry measure, and the tenth of the gomor will be in fair proportion to the gomor. 
\v 12 The \f + \fr 45:12 \fqa Gr. \ft στάθμιον standard-weight\f*standard shekel will be twenty obols, five shekels will be five, and ten shekels ten, and fifty shekels will be your mina. 
\p
\v 13 These are the first-fruits which you will offer; a sixth part of a gomor of wheat, and the sixth part of it \add will consist\add* of an ephah from a cor of barley. 
\v 14 And \add you will give as\add* the appointed measure of oil one bath of oil out of ten baths; for ten baths are a gomor. 
\v 15 One sheep from the flock out of ten, as an oblation from all the tribes of Israel, for sacrifices, and for whole-burnt-offerings, and for peace-offerings, to make atonement for you, says the Lord God. 
\v 16 All the people will give these first-fruits to the prince of Israel. 
\p
\v 17 Through the prince will be \add offered\add* the whole-burnt-offerings and the food-offerings, and the drink-offerings in the feasts, and at the new moons, and on the sabbaths; and in all the feasts of the house of Israel: he will offer the sin-offerings, and the food-offering, and the whole-burnt-offerings, and the peace-offerings, to make atonement for the house of Israel. 
\p
\v 18 Thus says the Lord God; In the first month, on the first \add day\add* of the month, you will take a calf without blemish out of the herd, to make atonement for the holy place. 
\v 19 The priest will take of the blood of the atonement, and put it on the thresholds of the house, and upon the four corners of the temple, and upon the altar, and upon the thresholds of the gate of the inner court. 
\v 20 Thus will you do in the seventh month; on the first \add day\add* of the month you will take a contribution from each one; and you will make atonement for the house. 
\p
\v 21 In the first \add month\add*, on the fourteenth \add day\add* of the month, you will have the feast of the passover; seven days will you eat unleavened bread. 
\v 22 The prince will offer in that day a calf for a sin-offering for himself, and the house, and for all the people of the land. 
\v 23 For the seven days of the feast he will offer as whole-burnt-offerings to the Lord seven calves and seven rams without blemish daily for the seven days; and a kid of the goats daily for a sin-offering, and a food-offering. 
\v 24 You will prepare a cake for the calf, and cakes for the ram, and a hin of oil for the cake. 
\v 25 In the seventh month, on the fifteenth \add day\add* of the month, you will sacrifice in the feast in the same way seven days, as \add they sacrificed\add* the sin-offerings, and the whole-burnt-offerings, and the freewill-offering, and the oil. 
\c 46 
\p
\v 1 Thus says the Lord God; The gate that is in the inner court, that looks eastward, will be shut the six working days; \add but\add* let it be opened on the sabbath-day, and it will be opened on the day of the new moon. 
\v 2 The prince will enter by the way of the porch of the inner gate, and will stand at the entrance of the gate, and the priests will prepare his whole-burnt-offerings and his peace-offerings, and he will worship at the entrance of the gate: then he will come forth; but the gate will not be shut till evening. 
\v 3 The people of the land will worship at the entrance of that gate, both on the sabbaths and at the new moons, before the Lord. 
\p
\v 4 The prince will offer whole-burnt-offerings to the Lord on the sabbath-day, six lambs without blemish, and a ram without blemish; 
\v 5 and a freewill-offering, a food-offering for the ram, and a food-offering for the lambs, the gift of his hand, and a hin of oil for the food-offering. 
\v 6 On the day of the new moon a calf without blemish, and six lambs, and there will be a ram without blemish; 
\v 7 and a food-offering for the ram, and there will be a food-offering for the calf as a freewill-offering, and for the lambs, according as his hand can furnish, and \add there will be\add* a hin of oil for the cake. 
\p
\v 8 When the prince goes in, he will go in by the way of the porch of the gate, and he will go forth by the way of the gate. 
\v 9 Whenever the people of the land will go in before the Lord at the feasts, he who goes in by the way of the north gate to worship will go forth by the way of the south gate; and he who goes in by the way of the south gate will go forth by the way of the north gate: he will not return by the gate by which he entered, but he will go forth opposite it. 
\v 10 The prince will enter with them among them when they go in; and when they go forth, he will go forth. 
\p
\v 11 In the feasts and in the general assemblies the freewill oblation will be a food-offering for the calf, and a food-offering for the ram, and for the lambs, as his hand can furnish, and a hin of oil for the food-offering. 
\v 12 If the prince should prepare \add as\add* a thanksgiving a whole-burnt-peace-offering to the Lord, and should open for himself the gate looking eastward, and offer his whole-burnt-offering, and his peace-offerings, as he does on the sabbath-day; then he will go out, and will shut the doors after he has gone out. 
\p
\v 13 He will prepare daily as a whole-burnt-offering to the Lord a lamb of a year old without blemish: in the morning he will prepare it. 
\v 14 He will prepare a freewill-offering for it in the morning, the sixth part of a measure \add of flour\add*, and a third part of a hin of oil to mix \add therewith\add* the fine flour, \add as\add* a freewill-offering to the Lord, a perpetual ordinance. 
\v 15 You will prepare the lamb, and the freewill-offering, and the oil in the morning, \add for\add* a perpetual whole-burnt-sacrifice. 
\p
\v 16 Thus says the Lord God; If the prince will give a gift to one of his sons out of his inheritance, this will be to his sons a possession \add as\add* an inheritance. 
\v 17 But if he give a gift to one of his servants, then it will belong to him until the year of release; and \add then\add* he will restore \add it\add* to the prince: but of the inheritance of his sons \add the possession\add* will continue to them. 
\v 18 The prince will by no means take of the inheritance of the people, to oppress them: he will give an inheritance to his sons out of his \add own\add* possession: that my people not be scattered, every one from his possession. 
\p
\v 19 He brought me into the entrance of the \add place\add* behind the gate, into the chamber of the sanctuary belonging to the priests, that looks toward the north: and, behold, there was a place set apart. 
\v 20 He said to me, This is the place where the priests will boil the trespass-offerings and the sin-offerings, and there will they bake the food-offering always; so as not to carry \add them\add* out into the outer court, to sanctify the people. 
\p
\v 21 He brought me into the outer court, and led me round upon the four sides of the court; and, behold, there was a court on \add each of\add* the sides of the court, 
\v 22 on \add every\add* side a court, \add even\add* a court for all the four \add sides\add*, and \add each\add* little court belonging to the court was in length forty cubits, and \add in\add* breadth thirty cubits, \add there was\add* one measure to the four. 
\v 23 And \add there were\add* chambers in them all around, all around the four, and cooking-places formed under the chambers all around. 
\v 24 He said to me, These are the cooks' houses, where those who serve the house will boil the sacrifices of the people. 
\c 47 
\p
\v 1 He brought me to the entrance of the house; and, behold, water issued from under the porch eastward, for the front of the house looked eastward; and the water came down from the right side, from the south to the altar. 
\v 2 He brought me out by the way of the northern gate, and he led me round by the way outside to the gate of the court that looks eastward; and, behold, water came down from the right side, 
\v 3 in \add the direction\add* in which a man went out opposite; and \add there was\add* a measuring line in his hand, and he measured a thousand \add cubits\add* with the measure; 
\v 4 and he passed through the water; \add it was\add* water of a fountain: and \add again\add* he measured a thousand, and passed through the water; and the water was up to the thighs: and \add again\add* he measured a thousand; and he passed through water up to the loins. 
\v 5 And \add again\add* he measured a thousand; and he could not pass through: for \add the water\add* rose as of a torrent which \add men\add* cannot pass over. 
\p
\v 6 He said to me, Have you seen \add this\add*, son of man? Then he brought me, and led me back to the brink of the river 
\v 7 as I returned; and, behold, on the brink of the river \add there were\add* very many trees on this side and on that side. 
\v 8 He said to me, This is the water that goes forth to Galilee that lies eastward, and it is gone down to Arabia, and has reached as far as to the sea to the outlet of the water: and it will heal the waters. 
\v 9 It will come to pass, \add that\add* every animal of living \add and\add* moving creatures, all on which the river will come, will live: and there will be there very many fish; for this water will go there, and it will heal \add them\add*, and they will live: everything on which the river will come will live. 
\p
\v 10 Fishers will stand there from Ingadin to Enagallim; it will be a place to spread out nets upon; it will be distinct; and the fish of it \add will be\add* as the fish of the great sea, a very great multitude. 
\v 11 But at the outlet of the water, and the turn of it, and where it overflows \add its banks\add*, they will not heal at all; they are given to salt. 
\v 12 Every fruit tree will grow by the river, \add even\add* on the bank of it on this side and on that side: they will not decay upon it, neither will their fruit fail: they will bring forth the first-fruit of their early crop, for these their waters come forth of the sanctuary: and their fruit will be for food, and their foliage for health. 
\p
\v 13 Thus says the Lord God; You will inherit these borders of the land; \add they are\add* given by lot to the twelve tribes of the children of Israel. 
\v 14 You will inherit it, each according to his brother's portion, \add even the land\add* concerning which I lifted up my hand to give \add it\add* to your fathers: and this land will fall to you by lot. 
\p
\v 15 These are the borders of the land that lies northward, from the great sea that comes down, and divides the entrance of Emaseldam; 
\v 16 Maabthera, Ebrameliam, between the coasts of Damascus and the coasts of Emathi, the habitation of Saunan, which \add places\add* are above the coasts of Auranitis. 
\v 17 These are the borders from the sea, from the habitations of Ænan, the coasts of Damascus, and the northern \add coasts\add*. 
\v 18 The eastern coasts between Loranitis, and Damascus, and the land of Gilead, and the land of Israel, the Jordan divides to the sea that is east of the city of palm-trees. These are the eastern \add coasts\add*. 
\v 19 The southern and south-western \add coasts are\add* from Thæman and the city of palm-trees, to the water of Marimoth Cadem, reaching forth to the great sea. This part is the south and south-west. 
\v 20 This part of the great sea forms a border, till \add one comes\add* opposite the entrance of Emath, \add even\add* as far as the entrance of it. These are the parts west of Emath. 
\p
\v 21 So you will divide this land to them, \add even\add* to the tribes of Israel. 
\v 22 You will cast the lot upon it, for yourselves and the strangers that sojourn among you, who have begotten children among you: and they will be to you as natives among the children of Israel; they will eat with you in \add their\add* inheritance among the tribes of Israel. 
\v 23 They will be in the tribe of proselytes among the proselytes that are with them: there will you give them an inheritance, says the Lord God. 
\c 48 
\p
\v 1 These are the names of the tribes from the northern corner, on the side of the descent that draws a line to the entrance of Emath the palace of Ælam, the border of Damascus northward on the side of Emath the palace; and they will have the eastern parts as far as the sea, for Dan, one \add portion\add*. 
\v 2 From the borders of Dan eastward as far as the west sea-coast, for Asser, one. 
\v 3 From the borders of Asser, from the eastern parts as far as the west coasts, for Naphtali, one. 
\v 4 From the borders of Naphtali, from the east as far as the west coasts, for Manasse, one. 
\v 5 From the borders of Manasse, from the eastern parts as far as the west coasts, for Ephraim, one. 
\v 6 From the borders of Ephraim, from the eastern parts to the west coasts, for Ruben, one. 
\v 7 From the borders of Ruben, from the eastern parts as far as the west coasts, for Judah, one. 
\p
\v 8 From the borders of Judah, from the eastern parts will be the offering of first-fruits, in breadth twenty-five thousand \add reeds\add*, and in length as one of the portions \add measured\add* from the east even to the western parts: and the sanctuary will be among them. 
\v 9 \add As for\add* the first-fruits which they will offer to the Lord, \add it will be\add* in length twenty-five thousand, and in breadth twenty-five thousand. 
\v 10 Out of this will be the first-fruits of the holy things to the priests, northward, twenty-five thousand, and towards the west, ten thousand, and southward, twenty-five thousand: and the mountain of the sanctuary, will be among it, 
\v 11 for the priests, for the consecrated sons of Sadduc, who keep the charges of the house, who didn't err in the error of the children of Israel, as the Levites erred. 
\v 12 The first-fruits will be given to them out of the first-fruits of the land, \add even\add* a most holy portion from the borders of the Levites. 
\p
\v 13 The Levites \add will have\add* the \add part\add*, next to the borders of the priests, in length twenty-five thousand, and in breadth ten thousand: the whole length \add will be\add* five and twenty thousand, and the breadth twenty thousand. 
\v 14 No \add part\add* of it will be sold, nor measured \add as for sale\add*, neither will the first-fruits of the land be taken away: for they are holy to the Lord. 
\p
\v 15 But \add concerning\add* the five thousand that remain in the breadth in the twenty-five thousand, they will be a suburb to the city for dwelling, and for a space before it: and the city will be in the midst of it. 
\v 16 These \add will be\add* its dimensions; from the northern side four thousand and five hundred, and from the southern side four thousand and five hundred, and from the eastern side four thousand and five hundred, and from the western side \add they will measure\add* four thousand five hundred. 
\v 17 There will be a space to the city northward two hundred and fifty, and southward two hundred and fifty, and eastward two hundred and fifty, and westward two hundred and fifty. 
\p
\v 18 The remainder of the length that is next to the first-fruits of the holy \add portion will be\add* ten thousand eastward, and ten thousand westward: and they will be the first-fruits of the sanctuary; and the fruits of it will be for bread to those who labour for the city. 
\v 19 Those who labour for the city will labour for it out of all the tribes of Israel. 
\p
\v 20 The whole offering \add will be\add* a square of twenty-five thousand by twenty-five thousand: you will separate \add again part\add* of it, the first-fruits of the sanctuary, from the possession of the city. 
\p
\v 21 The prince \add will have\add* the remainder on this side and on that side from the first-fruits of the sanctuary, and \add there will be\add* a possession of the city, for twenty-five thousand cubits in length, to the eastern and western borders, for twenty-five thousand to the western borders, next to the portions of the prince; and the first-fruits of the holy things and the sanctuary of the house \add will be\add* among it. 
\v 22 There will be \add a portion taken\add* from the Levites, from the possession of the city among the princes between the borders of Judah and the borders of Benjamin, and it will be \add the portion\add* of the princes. 
\p
\v 23 And \add as for\add* the rest of the tribes, from the eastern parts as far as the western, Benjamin \add will have\add* one \add portion\add*. 
\v 24 From the borders of Benjamin, from the eastern parts to the western, Symeon, one. 
\v 25 From the borders of Symeon, from the eastern parts to the western, Issachar, one. 
\v 26 From the borders of Issachar, from the eastern parts to the western, Zebulun, one. 
\v 27 From the borders of Zebulun, from the east to the western parts, Gad, one. 
\v 28 From the borders of Gad, from the eastern to the south-western parts; his coasts will even be from Thæman, and the water of Barimoth Cades, for an inheritance, to the great sea. 
\v 29 This is the land, which you will divide by lot to the tribes of Israel, and these are their portions, says the Lord God. 
\p
\v 30 These are the goings out of the city northward, four thousand and five hundred by measure. 
\v 31 The gates of the city \add will be\add* after the names of the tribes of Israel: three gates northward; the gate of Ruben, one, and the gate of Judah, one, and the gate of Levi, one. 
\v 32 Eastward four thousand and five hundred: and three gates; the gate of Joseph, one, and the gate of Benjamin, one, and the gate of Dan, one. 
\v 33 Southward, four thousand and five hundred by measure: and three gates; the gate of Symeon, one, and the gate of Issachar, one, and the gate of Zebulun, one. 
\v 34 Westward, four thousand and five hundred by measure: \add and\add* three gates; the gate of Gad, one, and the gate of Asser, one, and the gate of Naphtali, one. 
\p
\v 35 The circumference, eighteen thousand \add measures\add*: and the name of the city, from the day that it will be finished, will be the name of it. 
